"Yegelos and Hoabna, too."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanGuardBlamesMountainClimb"
msgid "10766"
msgstr ""
"That wasn't a fair fight...\n"
"I was all worn out from the\n"
"climb... How could I fight?{page_break}"
"How did Hoabna manage\n"
"to fight after climbing a\n"
"mountain like that!?"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "MsgShamanMoapaAsksVictorsNames"
msgid "10767"
msgstr ""
"You have defeated me, and\n"
"yet I still don't know your\n"
"names... Would you tell me?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10768"
msgstr ""
"A warrior who does not\n"
"share his name is a\n"
"humble warrior indeed."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10769"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, {actor_name:6}, {actor_name:7},\n"
"and {actor_name:8}. I shall remember\n"
"those names.{page_break}"
"We do not forget the names\n"
"of heroes who can defeat\n"
"me in fair combat."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanMoapaWantsToKnowNames"
msgid "10770"
msgstr ""
"Moapa said that he doesn't\n"
"even know the names of the\n"
"heroes who beat him...{page_break}"
"He feels bad for not having\n"
"asked. Maybe you should\n"
"go tell him your names."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanFormalBattleNeedsNames"
msgid "10771"
msgstr ""
"In a formal battle, it is both\n"
"customary and honorable to\n"
"give your name.{page_break}"
"It's not too late for you...\n"
"Please go tell my father\n"
"your names."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanNamesDoNotMatter"
msgid "10772"
msgstr ""
"Why does it matter if you\n"
"know the name of someone\n"
"who beat you or not?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanVictorsDeserveRespect"
msgid "10773"
msgstr ""
"If a warrior beats you, you\n"
"must learn his name...{page_break}"
"Not many people have beaten\n"
"me, and they deserve my\n"
"respect."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanShameNotKnowingVictors"
msgid "10774"
msgstr ""
"I would feel bad not knowing\n"
"the name of a warrior who\n"
"defeated me, I guess..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanFatherLostToRudeOutsiders"
msgid "10775"
msgstr ""
"What a shame... My own father,\n"
"losing to some ignorant\n"
"foreigner with bad manners."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanNamesBeforeBattleOldFashioned"
msgid "10776"
msgstr ""
"It's so old-fashioned to have\n"
"to give your name to an\n"
"opponent before a battle."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10777"
msgstr ""
"I'll never forget the name\n"
"of anyone I fight."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanWarehouseOwnerFeelsResponsible"
msgid "10778"
msgstr ""
"I was stunned to hear that\n"
"Moapa lost his battle...{page_break}"
"His weapons all came from\n"
"my own warehouse, so I feel\n"
"a little responsible."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanWelcomeContigoHero"
msgid "10779"
msgstr ""
"Everyone is depressed that\n"
"Moapa lost his big fight. They\n"
"should be glad the hero came!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanWeaponsDidNotCauseLoss"
msgid "10780"
msgstr ""
"Although it's not right to\n"
"blame his loss on the\n"
"weapons he used.{page_break}"
"I couldn't afford it if that\n"
"rumor started going around."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanHusbandWorriesAboutWeapons"
msgid "10781"
msgstr ""
"My husband is getting neurotic,\n"
"worrying about whether his\n"
"weapons caused the loss."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "MsgShamanVisitorsHaveTraveledFar"
msgid "10782"
msgstr ""
"You've traveled to lots of\n"
"different lands, haven't you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10783"
msgstr ""
"That explains it... The only\n"
"reason you won is because\n"
"of your travels...{page_break}"
"Your strange, exotic\n"
"weapons are what won\n"
"the day, not your skill."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10784"
msgstr ""
"I could have sworn that\n"
"fancy boat was yours...{page_break}"
"If you can afford such a\n"
"nice boat, you can probably\n"
"afford nice weapons, too."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanForgiveUnkindVillagers"
msgid "10785"
msgstr ""
"We're very fond of Moapa\n"
"here. He's a great leader.{page_break}"
"If anyone in town says\n"
"something mean to you,\n"
"please forgive them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanEnjoyGettingOutside"
msgid "10786"
msgstr ""
"I've been locked up inside\n"
"all day! I'm so glad to get\n"
"outside and stretch!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanPlanPicnicMeal"
msgid "10787"
msgstr ""
"Ah... I've been inside for so\n"
"long... I think I'll have a little\n"
"picnic! But what should I eat..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanSimpleMeatPotatoesBeans"
msgid "10788"
msgstr ""
"Around here, people like a\n"
"nice hot steak and some\n"
"potatoes and beans...{page_break}"
"You foreigners might be used\n"
"to strange, exotic food, but\n"
"we like our meals simple."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanMoapaMiserableAfterDefeat"
msgid "10789"
msgstr ""
"Moapa has been miserable\n"
"since his defeat. If only I could\n"
"have taken his place up there."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanVillagersWorryTooMuch"
msgid "10790"
msgstr ""
"It drives me nuts how\n"
"worked up everyone gets\n"
"about Moapa around here."

msgctxt "MsgShamanChildrenIgnoreTradition"
msgid "10791"
msgstr ""
"All of the older people in town\n"
"are really upset that Moapa\n"
"lost...{page_break}"
"It doesn't matter to us kids.\n"
"I think they're too hung up\n"
"on tradition.{end_wait} "

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanEagerForDinner"
msgid "10792"
msgstr ""
"I'm starving! I can't wait until\n"
"dinner! I love my meat and\n"
"potatoes! And BEANS!!!{page_break}"
"It must be the spices the\n"
"chef uses... Lots of salt,\n"
"and lots of pepper!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanSaltAndPepperOnly"
msgid "10793"
msgstr ""
"Those fancy foreign chefs\n"
"use all sorts of spices to\n"
"hide the flavor of their food.{page_break}"
"As far as I'm concerned,\n"
"there are only two spices:\n"
"salt and pepper."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanMoapaDefeatIncredible"
msgid "10794"
msgstr ""
"You beat Moapa? Incredible!\n"
"...Not that I ever doubted you!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanThreatenContigoRematch"
msgid "10795"
msgstr ""
"Don't be too pleased with\n"
"yourself for beating Moapa.{page_break}"
"One of these days, we'll\n"
"come storming into Contigo,\n"
"and we'll show you what's what!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanPrayForShamanWarrior"
msgid "10796"
msgstr ""
"Oh, please... Let a true\n"
"warrior be born in Shaman.\n"
"Let us forget this disgrace!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanFearRenewedContigoWar"
msgid "10797"
msgstr ""
"The older folks of Shaman\n"
"are quite upset that Moapa\n"
"was beaten.{page_break}"
"I'm afraid this might lead\n"
"to renewed fighting between\n"
"Shaman and Contigo."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanMoapaMustHaveBeenHungry"
msgid "10798"
msgstr ""
"Moapa must have been\n"
"hungry after climbing the\n"
"mountain...{page_break}"
"That's the only way those\n"
"lousy Contigo nobodies\n"
"could have beaten him."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanPrayForContigoConqueror"
msgid "10799"
msgstr ""
"I can't forgive the fact\n"
"that Contigo's heroes beat\n"
"our leader, Moapa...{page_break}"
"I hope a new hero is born in\n"
"Shaman, one who can crush\n"
"those Contigo barbarians..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanMoapaNeverForgetsVictor"
msgid "10800"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, the hero of Contigo!\n"
"I shall never forget you, the\n"
"only one that defeated me!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShamanVictorsNamesOnTrialColumns"
msgid "10801"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, {actor_name:6}, {actor_name:7},\n"
"and {actor_name:8}... I won't forget\n"
"those names...{page_break}"
"Someday, their names will be\n"
"engraved on the columns\n"
"leading to Trial Road."

msgctxt "MsgAhhhh2"
msgid "10802"
msgstr "Ahhhh!!!"

msgctxt "message"
msgid "10803"
msgstr "{actor_name:4}!"

msgctxt "message"
msgid "10804"
msgstr "Noooo!!!"

msgctxt "message"
msgid "10805"
msgstr "Oof!"

msgctxt "message"
msgid "10806"
msgstr "{actor_name:4}!"

msgctxt "message"
msgid "10807"
msgstr "{actor_name:2}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10808"
msgstr ""
"Is that...{pause_20_skippable} It's {actor_name:1}\n"
"and the others!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10809"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}? Isn't he a friend\n"
"of yours, {actor_name:5}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10810"
msgstr ""
"They both come from Vale, and\n"
"regardless of what {actor_name:1}\n"
"believes, they must be allies now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10811"
msgstr ""
"Don't be that way! You two have\n"
"much in common, even if you are\n"
"at odds right now..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10812"
msgstr ""
"But {actor_name:1} and the others\n"
"came all this way just to try\n"
"and stop us!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10813"
msgstr ""
"But didn't you hear that? It\n"
"sounded like a cry for help...\n"
"What if they're in trouble?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10814"
msgstr ""
"Hang on, {actor_name:4}!\n"
"Don't worry, {actor_name:2}!\n"
"Everything will be fine!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10815"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry about me... I'm\n"
"fine, but {actor_name:2}..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10816"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:2}, you're only using\n"
"one arm to hang on...\n"
"What's the matter?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10817"
msgstr ""
"I don't know... I think I hurt my\n"
"arm when I fell... It's totally\n"
"numb! I can't move it!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10818"
msgstr ""
"You shouldn't have tried\n"
"to save me when I fell\n"
"into that hole..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10819"
msgstr ""
"Oh, {actor_name:4}, don't blame\n"
"yourself... I wasn't going to\n"
"leave you down there!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10820"
msgstr ""
"It's no use! I can't pull\n"
"you up, {actor_name:2}! I'm\n"
"not strong enough!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10821"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}, please! You've\n"
"got to save {actor_name:2}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10822"
msgstr ""
"This doesn't look good...\n"
"We have to save {actor_name:2},\n"
"and fast!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10823"
msgstr ""
"No, I'm afraid you won't\n"
"be doing that..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10824"
msgstr "Who are you!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10825"
msgstr "Me? Why, I'm Karst."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10826"
msgstr "And I'm Agatio."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10827"
msgstr ""
"If you're not here to help my\n"
"friend, then get out of my\n"
"way, so I can do it myself!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10828"
msgstr ""
"Your friends will have to take\n"
"care of themselves. You have\n"
"a little debt to repay."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10829"
msgstr ""
"Debt? What are you talking\n"
"about? We've never even\n"
"seen you before!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10830"
msgstr ""
"Regardless, you have done Karst\n"
"here a great wrong, and you're\n"
"beginning to be a hindrance to us."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10831"
msgstr ""
"Wait a second... You two look\n"
"familiar somehow... Do you\n"
"know Saturos and Menardi?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10832"
msgstr ""
"So, you're not such a fool\n"
"after all, {actor_name:1}! You are\n"
"right. We are of the same clan.{page_break}"
"The Fire Clan, from the frozen\n"
"land of Prox, far to the north!{end_wait}"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10833"
msgstr "Prox? Never heard of it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10834"
msgstr ""
"That doesn't surprise me.\n"
"Our town hangs on the\n"
"brink of extinction."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10835"
msgstr ""
"And the seal placed on\n"
"Alchemy is responsible!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10836"
msgstr ""
"What are you saying? That\n"
"doesn't make any sense."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10837"
msgstr ""
"It matters not! For soon, Prox\n"
"will recover its lost power..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10838"
msgstr ""
"We shall bring Prox back from\n"
"the edge, and then all the people\n"
"of Weyard will kneel before us!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10839"
msgstr ""
"You think we'd let you, after\n"
"hearing all that nonsense?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10840"
msgstr "See! You're a hindrance!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10841"
msgstr ""
"And {actor_name:5} was trying\n"
"to help you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10842"
msgstr ""
"Actually...we don't know what\n"
"{actor_name:5}'s objectives are."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10843"
msgstr ""
"And we don't care, as long\n"
"as he lights the beacon on\n"
"Jupiter Lighthouse."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10844"
msgstr ""
"Then get out of our way!\n"
"We're here to stop {actor_name:5}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10845"
msgstr ""
"Move, or we'll have to\n"
"move you ourselves!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10846"
msgstr ""
"Did you hear that, Karst?\n"
"They actually want to fight?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10847"
msgstr ""
"You mean to tell us that\n"
"you would leave your\n"
"friend...hanging?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10848"
msgstr ""
"So this was all part\n"
"of your plan?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10849"
msgstr ""
"Cowards! Stop playing\n"
"dirty and fight fair!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10850"
msgstr ""
"If you really are the brats who\n"
"killed Saturos and Menardi, then\n"
"you've earned some new foes!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10851"
msgstr ""
"But answer me this: would\n"
"you still cry foul if you were\n"
"fighting us four on two?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10852"
msgstr ""
"That's why you were waiting\n"
"up here? To set a trap and\n"
"make {actor_name:4} and {actor_name:2} fall?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10853"
msgstr ""
"We didn't plan on snaring\n"
"both of them, though... That\n"
"{text_effect:2}was{reset_text_style} a pleasant surprise!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10854"
msgstr ""
"So that's the deal, is it?\n"
"You came up here to fight us?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10855"
msgstr ""
"Oh, did you figure that out all\n"
"on your own? Impressive! I'm\n"
"quite fond of intelligent boys..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10856"
msgstr ""
"I hope you don't think\n"
"we're afraid of a fair\n"
"fight, two on two..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10857"
msgstr "A fair fight?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10858"
msgstr ""
"I'm sorry if I misled you, but we\n"
"have a third... A Water Adept...\n"
"Alex!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10859"
msgstr "Alex?{pause_20_skippable} ...Where is he?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10860"
msgstr "What's wrong, Karst?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10861"
msgstr "It's Alex! He's gone!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10862"
msgstr "What!?"

msgctxt "message"
msgid "10863"
msgstr "Alex!"

msgctxt "message"
msgid "10864"
msgstr "Alex?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10865"
msgstr ""
"Did anyone see where\n"
"he went?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10866"
msgstr ""
"Forget about him! Honestly, I\n"
"was planning to do the same to\n"
"him that I'm about to do to them!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10867"
msgstr ""
"My only regret is that I\n"
"won't be able to wipe that\n"
"sneering smile off his face."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10868"
msgstr ""
"Well, take out all of your\n"
"aggressions on these brats...\n"
"You'll feel better!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10869"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}! Agatio and Karst\n"
"are attacking {actor_name:1}\n"
"and the others!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10870"
msgstr ""
"Do you think {actor_name:1} and\n"
"{actor_name:3} can handle them\n"
"without {actor_name:4} and {actor_name:2}'s help?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10871"
msgstr ""
"I'm disgusted that Karst\n"
"would set a trap for them.\n"
"It's dishonorable!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10872"
msgstr ""
"What if {actor_name:2} loses his\n"
"grip while they're still fighting?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10873"
msgstr ""
"There's still time! We have to\n"
"help {actor_name:1}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgFieldWaitingForCompanion"
msgid "10874"
msgstr ""
"Ah, {actor_name:5}... I've been\n"
"waiting for you."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10875"
msgstr ""
"Have you come here to\n"
"light the beacon?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10876"
msgstr ""
"And you're sure that's\n"
"{text_effect:2}all{reset_text_style} you're going to do?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10877"
msgstr ""
"Hmph. They consider you their\n"
"enemy, and yet you pity them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10878"
msgstr ""
"I saw you watching when\n"
"{actor_name:1}'s friends fell\n"
"into Karst's trap."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10879"
msgstr ""
"I know you, {actor_name:5}.{pause_20_skippable}\n"
"I know that if you leave\n"
"{actor_name:1} behind, you'll regret it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10880"
msgstr ""
"You're not like me. You can't\n"
"simply discard someone who\n"
"is no longer of use to you."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10881"
msgstr ""
"Well, you'd better hurry if you\n"
"still hope to save them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10882"
msgstr "Everyone recovered fully."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10883"
msgstr ""
"There you go! Consider it a\n"
"gift. You can still make it.\n"
"Go on..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgFieldFollowTrueFeelings"
msgid "10884"
msgstr ""
"It is time you followed your\n"
"true feelings. Go on.\n"
"Save your friends."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgFieldPartWithAgatio"
msgid "10885"
msgstr ""
"Even now, I want to run to\n"
"{actor_name:4}, to give her my aid...\n"
"It seems I am weak as well...{page_break}"
"I suppose I have no choice\n"
"but to part ways with Agatio\n"
"and Karst."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIMSorry"
msgid "10886"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}... I'm sorry...\n"
"I can't take any more..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10887"
msgstr "Keep it together, {actor_name:3}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10888"
msgstr ""
"Ha! You're a fool! Never let\n"
"concern distract you in battle!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10889"
msgstr "AHHHHHHHH!!!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWeDidItAgatio"
msgid "10890"
msgstr "We did it, Agatio!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10891"
msgstr "It was close, but we did it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10892"
msgstr ""
"Heh... He's no warrior. His\n"
"concern for his friend gave\n"
"us the opportunity to strike!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10893"
msgstr ""
"What's this? He's still alive!?\n"
"Even after that blow?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10894"
msgstr ""
"It would be a shame if you\n"
"and I ever had to regret letting\n"
"him live..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10895"
msgstr "{actor_name:1}! Watch out!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10896"
msgstr ""
"He's still alive! If we're going to\n"
"act, {actor_name:5}, we have to act now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10897"
msgstr "They're going to kill {actor_name:1}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10898"
msgstr ""
"No, they aren't! I'm not about\n"
"to let that happen!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10899"
msgstr "None of us are, {actor_name:6}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10900"
msgstr "{actor_name:5}? What's going on?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10901"
msgstr ""
"Be grateful! We just\n"
"did you a favor!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10902"
msgstr ""
"I understand that when Venus\n"
"was lit, the ground shook so\n"
"fiercely that the very earth split.{page_break}"
"Curious that it hasn't here!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10903"
msgstr ""
"You haven't lit the beacon\n"
"yet, have you? And after all\n"
"we've done to help you!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10904"
msgstr ""
"We're going to light the\n"
"beacon right now..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10905"
msgstr ""
"If that's true, then you'd\n"
"better go do it!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10906"
msgstr ""
"But we're not leaving\n"
"{actor_name:1} behind."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10907"
msgstr ""
"Oh, great... Are you going\n"
"to betray us now?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10908"
msgstr ""
"Typical. And you're going to\n"
"try to stop us from finishing\n"
"them off, aren't you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10909"
msgstr ""
"Don't lie... We can see it in\n"
"your eyes. We can see what\n"
"you truly mean to do."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10910"
msgstr ""
"If you're only here to clear\n"
"the way for us to light the\n"
"beacon, then your work is done."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10911"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1} has proven to\n"
"be a greater foe than we'd\n"
"imagined. We can't let him live."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10912"
msgstr ""
"Consider how powerful these two\n"
"were without the aid of a Water\n"
"Adept. We have to finish them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10913"
msgstr ""
"If you want them, you're going\n"
"to have to face us first!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10914"
msgstr ""
"You're both quite badly\n"
"injured... You're in no shape\n"
"to fight all four of them.{page_break}"
"I think it would be best\n"
"if you left now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10915"
msgstr "We haven't much choice..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10916"
msgstr "Karst, no!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10917"
msgstr ""
"Agatio, if we fight {actor_name:5}\n"
"now...we'll be destroyed."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10918"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1} killed your sister!\n"
"Where is your anger!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10919"
msgstr ""
"I am filled with rage, but not so\n"
"much as to be blinded by it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10920"
msgstr "What, then? Do we give up?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10921"
msgstr "Fine! But this is not the end."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10922"
msgstr ""
"Do with {actor_name:1}\n"
"as you will."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10923"
msgstr ""
"But swear this oath to us:\n"
"if we leave now, you will\n"
"light the beacon's fire."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10924"
msgstr ""
"I don't care if you want to\n"
"help {actor_name:2} or not!\n"
"The lighthouse comes first!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10925"
msgstr ""
"We do not have time to wait\n"
"for you to save {actor_name:2}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10926"
msgstr ""
"Go, {actor_name:5}.\n"
"I will tend to {actor_name:2}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10927"
msgstr ""
"And be sure to bring with\n"
"you the Mars Star that\n"
"{actor_name:1} carries on him."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10928"
msgstr ""
"How did you know\n"
"about the Mars Star?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10929"
msgstr ""
"Did you think this was about\n"
"nothing more than revenge?\n"
"Alex told us about it!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10930"
msgstr ""
"Take the Mars Star, or we'll\n"
"be forced to make you!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10931"
msgstr ""
"Do not force our\n"
"hand on this!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10932"
msgstr "Go on, {actor_name:5}. Take it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10933"
msgstr ""
"I don't know why you're doing\n"
"this, but I trust you...\n"
"Take the Mars Star."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10934"
msgstr "{actor_name:5} took the Mars Star."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10935"
msgstr ""
"That's better, {actor_name:5}.\n"
"We'll be waiting for you\n"
"on the aerie."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10936"
msgstr "{actor_name:5}, wait..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10937"
msgstr ""
"We cannot trust them.\n"
"Take me with you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10938"
msgstr ""
"Good thinking. If something\n"
"happens up there, you'll be\n"
"safer with {actor_name:8}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10939"
msgstr ""
"We'll be fine. Take\n"
"{actor_name:8} with you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10940"
msgstr ""
"Listen to the others...\n"
"Safety in numbers, as\n"
"they say..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgNoWhyAre"
msgid "10941"
msgstr ""
"{control_28:5}{page_break}"
", {actor_name:5}... No!\n"
"Why are you helping them?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgDonTWorry"
msgid "10942"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry about us... Help\n"
"{actor_name:2} and {actor_name:4} first."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWeHaveTo"
msgid "10943"
msgstr ""
"We have to help {actor_name:2}.\n"
"He can't hold on for much\n"
"longer."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIDonT"
msgid "10944"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}! I don't know how\n"
"you survived that attack,\n"
"but I'm so glad you did...{page_break}"
"We're going to help you...\n"
"We're going to heal you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgYouVeBeen"
msgid "10945"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:3}... You've been injured.\n"
"Don't worry about the others.\n"
"Let's take care of those wounds."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10946"
msgstr ""
"Why did you help us, {actor_name:5}?\n"
"Whatever it was, I'm glad you\n"
"stopped to help us...{page_break}"
"But why do you have to\n"
"still light the beacon?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10947"
msgstr ""
"I thought you were our\n"
"enemy, {actor_name:5}... Why did\n"
"you stop to help us?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10948"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:2} and {actor_name:4} are\n"
"back. They fell through that\n"
"hole, and then this panel..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10949"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}! Look at you!\n"
"You're a mess! I thought I'd\n"
"never see you again..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10950"
msgstr ""
"You're pretty tough for your\n"
"age... I'm impressed, {actor_name:3}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgYouReLate"
msgid "10951"
msgstr "You're late, {actor_name:5}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10952"
msgstr "Now light the beacon!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgOnceYouVe"
msgid "10953"
msgstr ""
"Once you've lit the beacon,\n"
"we might even forgive you\n"
"for saving {actor_name:1} back there."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgOnceJupiterIs"
msgid "10954"
msgstr ""
"Once Jupiter is lit, only\n"
"Mars remains! Now, light\n"
"the beacon!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgOnceJupiterIsLit"
msgid "10955"
msgstr ""
"Once Jupiter is lit, we'll have no\n"
"need for you. Just watch..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgDoEvenThink"
msgid "10956"
msgstr ""
"Do even think about\n"
"resisting us... We have\n"
"our own ideas about that.{page_break}"
"Once the beacon is lit,\n"
"your usefulness will have\n"
"run out for good."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "MsgThereSeemsTo"
msgid "10957"
msgstr ""
"There seems to be a wide\n"
"hole for the Elemental Star.{page_break}"
"Cast the Jupiter Star in?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWeHaveIgnited"
msgid "10958"
msgstr ""
"We have ignited the beacon...\n"
"The third lighthouse is lit...\n"
"Now let us go..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10959"
msgstr "I don't think so..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10960"
msgstr ""
"You see, you've betrayed\n"
"us once already..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10961"
msgstr ""
"We simply can't trust\n"
"you anymore..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10962"
msgstr ""
"And now that Jupiter\n"
"Lighthouse is lit, I'm afraid we\n"
"have little use for traitors."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10963"
msgstr ""
"Poor dear... You look puzzled.\n"
"Would you like to know\n"
"why we don't need you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10964"
msgstr ""
"I'd be happy to tell you. Mars\n"
"Lighthouse{pause_20_skippable} is in Prox."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10965"
msgstr ""
"Figured it out, have you?\n"
"Yes, Mars Lighthouse is in\n"
"Prox."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10966"
msgstr "What are you doing!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10967"
msgstr "They stole the Mars Star!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10968"
msgstr "Your job is done now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10969"
msgstr "We're not done yet..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10970"
msgstr ""
"We've got the Mars Star!\n"
"We don't need you anymore!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10971"
msgstr ""
"You know what that means,\n"
"of course, don't you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10972"
msgstr ""
"Exactly! That means it's\n"
"time to die, {actor_name:5}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10973"
msgstr ""
"No? Well, how can I put this?\n"
"It's time to die!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10974"
msgstr ""
"But what will happen to\n"
"{actor_name:5}'s parents?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10975"
msgstr ""
"We keep our promises! Once all\n"
"four lighthouses have been\n"
"lit, we shall release them!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10976"
msgstr ""
"We would never do anything as\n"
"terrible as breaking our word...\n"
"as you have done so casually."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10977"
msgstr ""
"But if you're dead...\n"
"Who will come to take\n"
"them home from Prox?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10978"
msgstr ""
"I guess they'll just have to spend\n"
"their remaining years in the\n"
"frozen wastelands of the north!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10979"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry! They'll be fine!\n"
"Now prepare for the end!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgBlank5"
msgid "10980"
msgstr "{actor_name:5}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10981"
msgstr ""
"I thought you were taking too\n"
"long, so I came to check on\n"
"you. What's going on?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10982"
msgstr ""
"They say they don't\n"
"need us anymore..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10983"
msgstr ""
"Agatio! {actor_name:5}'s sister isn't\n"
"supposed to be here..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10984"
msgstr ""
"What do you want me to\n"
"do? We can't just leave\n"
"now! We have to finish them!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10985"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry, {actor_name:5}!\n"
"I'm here to help!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgBlank6"
msgid "10986"
msgstr "{actor_name:6}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10987"
msgstr ""
"I got the feeling something was\n"
"wrong, so I rushed up here. Just\n"
"in the nick of time, it looks like!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10988"
msgstr ""
"Thank you, {actor_name:7}! I'm\n"
"not looking forward to fighting,\n"
"but I'm glad you're here."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10989"
msgstr ""
"Another one? Agatio, we're\n"
"rapidly being outnumbered!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10990"
msgstr ""
"It's too late to flee now! We\n"
"have to keep fighting!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10991"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1} and the others\n"
"are safe! Now let's take care\n"
"of these two rats!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWeDidItWe"
msgid "10992"
msgstr ""
"We did it...\n"
"We beat them..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10993"
msgstr "Barely..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10994"
msgstr "What should we do with them?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10995"
msgstr "Finish us!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10996"
msgstr ""
"But think: what happens to\n"
"your parents if neither we nor\n"
"Saturos and Menardi return?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10997"
msgstr ""
"Are you saying your people\n"
"will kill our parents if you don't\n"
"return to Prox? I doubt that!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10998"
msgstr ""
"Well then, I suppose you'd\n"
"better finish us off, like I said."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "10999"
msgstr ""
"What's the matter? Are you\n"
"going to do it or not?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11000"
msgstr "No, {actor_name:5}! Don't!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11001"
msgstr ""
"You've made the better\n"
"choice, {actor_name:5}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11002"
msgstr "When did you get here, Alex?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11003"
msgstr ""
"If Karst is not bluffing... If you\n"
"kill them, all of your efforts\n"
"will have been for naught."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11004"
msgstr ""
"Do you understand, {actor_name:5}?\n"
"If that happens, {actor_name:1} will\n"
"suffer the same fate you do..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11005"
msgstr "Alex! What are you doing!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11006"
msgstr "I have revived them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11007"
msgstr ""
"Why!? Are you going to make\n"
"us fight them again?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11008"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry, {actor_name:6}.\n"
"Look at them... They can barely\n"
"walk right now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11009"
msgstr ""
"Still, that doesn't give you\n"
"the right to..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11010"
msgstr ""
"If you're not going to finish\n"
"them off, you'll just be leaving\n"
"them here, won't you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11011"
msgstr ""
"You're not going to help\n"
"us defeat these brats?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11012"
msgstr ""
"You'd better not be expecting\n"
"a big thank-you for this, Alex!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11013"
msgstr ""
"Of course not, Karst.\n"
"I would never ask for\n"
"your gratitude."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11014"
msgstr ""
"What's keeping {actor_name:5}\n"
"and the others?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11015"
msgstr ""
"We should be going before\n"
"{actor_name:1} and the others arrive."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11016"
msgstr ""
"If they're coming up, how do\n"
"you plan on avoiding them\n"
"on your way down?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11017"
msgstr ""
"Do not worry about us...\n"
"We'll just take the elevator."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11018"
msgstr ""
"Now that the lighthouse has\n"
"been lit, it should be fully\n"
"operational again."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11019"
msgstr "Oh! You're looking better!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11020"
msgstr "{actor_name:5}, {actor_name:6}..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11021"
msgstr "{actor_name:1}... {actor_name:2}..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11022"
msgstr ""
"Man! They got away!\n"
"What a bunch of jerks!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11023"
msgstr ""
"All right, {actor_name:5}! We want\n"
"to know what's going on!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11024"
msgstr ""
"It's all quite complicated,\n"
"{actor_name:1}. There are a number\n"
"of{pause_20_skippable} extenuating circumstances."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11025"
msgstr ""
"What are you talking\n"
"about, Kraden?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11026"
msgstr ""
"Look, I don't think any of\n"
"us are in any shape for\n"
"another fight right now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11027"
msgstr "What do you mean, {actor_name:3}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11028"
msgstr ""
"I'm just saying we should\n"
"get ourselves back to Contigo\n"
"and sort things out there."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11029"
msgstr ""
"That's a sound plan, {actor_name:3}...\n"
"I fully agree."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11030"
msgstr ""
"You're right. We can't fight\n"
"right now. Let's head back\n"
"to Contigo.{page_break}"
"What do you say, {actor_name:5}?\n"
"Can we talk there?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11031"
msgstr ""
"We'll be waiting for you...\n"
"So don't think you can\n"
"sneak off again!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11032"
msgstr ""
"He's right, {actor_name:5}. It's time\n"
"we explained ourselves to them.\n"
"We should go to Contigo."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11033"
msgstr ""
"We'll be there, {actor_name:1}.\n"
"I promise. I hope you can\n"
"still trust me."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11034"
msgstr ""
"I've never stopped trusting\n"
"you, {actor_name:6}. I'll be waiting\n"
"for you in Contigo."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11035"
msgstr ""
"We'll be expecting you. Don't\n"
"think you can sneak out of this!\n"
"You owe us an explanation!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWasnTThe"
msgid "11036"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1} wasn't the only\n"
"surprise. They were all far more\n"
"powerful than I'd expected."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11037"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry, Karst! We'll win\n"
"in the end..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11038"
msgstr ""
"This one moved... I can't\n"
"believe they're still alive!\n"
"The pests!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11039"
msgstr ""
"If we stay here much longer,\n"
"{actor_name:1} and the others\n"
"will come! We should leave!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11040"
msgstr ""
"I know... But treason deserves\n"
"death! We must finish them!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11041"
msgstr ""
"There's no time for\n"
"petty grudges!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11042"
msgstr "Alex! You..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11043"
msgstr ""
"You no longer consider me\n"
"a friend? I do not care."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11044"
msgstr ""
"It goes beyond that, Alex!\n"
"You've betrayed us, and\n"
"treason deserves death!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11045"
msgstr ""
"Yes, I heard you the first time.{page_break}"
"But shouldn't you heal\n"
"yourselves before making\n"
"foolish threats?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11046"
msgstr ""
"After fighting both {actor_name:1}\n"
"and {actor_name:5}, you're in no\n"
"condition to fight me."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11047"
msgstr ""
"And if {actor_name:1} and the others\n"
"come, what chance will you have?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11048"
msgstr ""
"What's keeping {actor_name:5}\n"
"and the others?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11049"
msgstr "There's no time to talk!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11050"
msgstr "Then what should we do?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11051"
msgstr ""
"We take the elevator! With\n"
"the beacon lit, it should be\n"
"fully operational once more."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11052"
msgstr "We have no choice. Let's go."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11053"
msgstr ""
"Good! You're listening to\n"
"reason! Now follow me!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11054"
msgstr "{actor_name:5}! {actor_name:6}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11055"
msgstr "What's happened?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11056"
msgstr ""
"It seems they fought with\n"
"Agatio and Karst..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11057"
msgstr ""
"I had a really bad feeling\n"
"after {actor_name:7} left.\n"
"I hate it when I'm right..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11058"
msgstr ""
"Your power of prediction must\n"
"be even stronger than you'd\n"
"thought, {actor_name:3}..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11059"
msgstr ""
"Blast! They must have taken\n"
"the elevator to escape!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11060"
msgstr ""
"How could they have done\n"
"that to {actor_name:6}? Those monsters!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11061"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5} tried to help us...\n"
"They must have attacked him\n"
"because he betrayed them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11062"
msgstr ""
"So, does that mean {actor_name:5}\n"
"isn't really our enemy?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11063"
msgstr "{actor_name:5}! You're alive!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11064"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:4}, he needs healing,\n"
"quickly! There's still time!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11065"
msgstr ""
"Don't let 'em die! {actor_name:5}\n"
"still has a lot of questions to\n"
"answer before he's in the clear!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11066"
msgstr ""
"If you save {actor_name:5}, we'll\n"
"tell you everything..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11067"
msgstr ""
"All right, {actor_name:5}! We want\n"
"to know what's going on!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11068"
msgstr ""
"It's all quite complicated,\n"
"{actor_name:1}. There are a number\n"
"of{pause_20_skippable} extenuating circumstances."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11069"
msgstr ""
"What are you talking\n"
"about, Kraden?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11070"
msgstr ""
"Look, I don't think any of\n"
"us are in any shape for\n"
"another fight right now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11071"
msgstr "What do you mean, {actor_name:3}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11072"
msgstr ""
"I'm just saying we should\n"
"get ourselves back to Contigo\n"
"and sort things out there."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11073"
msgstr ""
"That's a sound plan, {actor_name:3}...\n"
"I fully agree."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11074"
msgstr ""
"You're right. We can't fight\n"
"right now. Let's head back\n"
"to Contigo.{page_break}"
"What do you say, {actor_name:5}?\n"
"Can we talk there?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11075"
msgstr ""
"We'll be waiting for you...\n"
"So don't think you can\n"
"sneak off again!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11076"
msgstr ""
"He's right, {actor_name:5}. It's time\n"
"we explained ourselves to them.\n"
"We should go to Contigo."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11077"
msgstr ""
"We'll be there, {actor_name:1}.\n"
"I promise. I hope you can\n"
"still trust me."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11078"
msgstr ""
"I've never stopped trusting\n"
"you, {actor_name:6}. I'll be waiting\n"
"for you in Contigo."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11079"
msgstr ""
"We'll be expecting you. Don't\n"
"think you can sneak out of this!\n"
"You owe us an explanation!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgFieldDoorLocked"
msgid "11080"
msgstr "The door's locked."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgFieldShowAnemosPower"
msgid "11081"
msgstr ""
"Holder of the star...\n"
"Show the power of Anemos!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11082"
msgstr ""
"You didn't warn me that there\n"
"would be an earthquake when\n"
"the beacon was lit!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11083"
msgstr ""
"The core is shining so\n"
"brightly already..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11084"
msgstr "I've heard tales of this..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11085"
msgstr ""
"But I had no idea it would\n"
"be so spectacular."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIVeHeard"
msgid "11086"
msgstr "I've heard tales of this..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11087"
msgstr ""
"But I had no idea it would\n"
"be so spectacular."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgYouReNot"
msgid "11088"
msgstr ""
"You're not planning on running\n"
"away from {actor_name:1} again, are you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11089"
msgstr ""
"We can't run anymore, {actor_name:5}.\n"
"I promised him that we wouldn't."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11090"
msgstr ""
"Besides, they want to talk,\n"
"not fight..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11091"
msgstr ""
"They're waiting for us.\n"
"Let's go to Contigo."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWeShouldnT"
msgid "11092"
msgstr ""
"We shouldn't run from {actor_name:1}\n"
"anymore, {actor_name:5}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo119"
msgid "11093"
msgstr ""
"Are you looking for {actor_name:1}?\n"
"He and his colleagues are in the\n"
"house at the top of the hill.{page_break}"
"Are you the people they've\n"
"been waiting for?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo120"
msgid "11094"
msgstr ""
"Everyone's left town for the\n"
"time being. They're transporting\n"
"the wings...{page_break}"
"Actually, they might even have\n"
"finished putting them onto the\n"
"ship by now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo121"
msgid "11095"
msgstr ""
"Is that your boat? It looks\n"
"exactly like the one in the\n"
"geoglyphs."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo122"
msgid "11096"
msgstr ""
"Jupiter Lighthouse has been lit,\n"
"for the first time in years...\n"
"Did you feel that earthquake?{page_break}"
"If that's what happens when\n"
"the lighthouses shine, I wish\n"
"that it had stayed dark!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo123"
msgid "11097"
msgstr ""
"They look like they're in\n"
"for some trouble. Oh well...\n"
"I ain't a'gonna help 'em."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo124"
msgid "11098"
msgstr ""
"The prophecies are all coming\n"
"true... We're living in some\n"
"strange times, it seems."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo125"
msgid "11099"
msgstr ""
"It's just like the legends said...\n"
"The ship in the geoglyphs has\n"
"finally come to Contigo."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo126"
msgid "11100"
msgstr ""
"What does it mean, when\n"
"ancient legends are turning\n"
"out to be true?{page_break}"
"I just want the world to go\n"
"back to the way it was before."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgGladYouKeptYourPromise"
msgid "11101"
msgstr ""
"I'm glad you kept your\n"
"promise, {actor_name:5}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11102"
msgstr ""
"All right, let's hear what he\n"
"has to say for himself!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11103"
msgstr ""
"What can we say, {actor_name:1}?\n"
"Has {actor_name:5} ever harmed you?\n"
"Have we ever fought against you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11104"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}'s been avoiding you,\n"
"but he never had any intention\n"
"of fighting you or anything..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11105"
msgstr ""
"And he definitely helped us out\n"
"back at Jupiter Lighthouse."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11106"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}'s been worrying about\n"
"{actor_name:6} nonstop since this\n"
"nightmare began!{page_break}"
"How could she run away\n"
"from him like that?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11107"
msgstr ""
"She was afraid that if we\n"
"met, we would be forced to\n"
"fight... She didn't want that."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11108"
msgstr ""
"I know that, now... But it doesn't\n"
"explain why you're doing this..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11109"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5} betrayed his hometown,\n"
"Vale... That's why he hasn't been\n"
"able to face {actor_name:1}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11110"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5} had hoped to play\n"
"the villain alone, without getting\n"
"{actor_name:6} or me involved..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11111"
msgstr ""
"He betrayed Vale? Kraden,\n"
"what are you talking about?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11112"
msgstr ""
"He conspired to steal the\n"
"Elemental Stars and fire the\n"
"beacons of the four lighthouses."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11113"
msgstr ""
"That's what Saturos and Menardi\n"
"were trying to do..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11114"
msgstr "Why were you helping them?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11115"
msgstr ""
"Our parents' lives were at\n"
"stake! We had to help!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11116"
msgstr ""
"Parents? But...your parents died\n"
"three years ago, in that storm..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11117"
msgstr ""
"That night, Saturos and his men\n"
"had raided Sol Sanctum... The\n"
"storm was their doing."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11118"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:2}, you saw two\n"
"strangers that night°Saturos\n"
"and Menardi.{page_break}"
"They were the only survivors\n"
"of Saturos's raiding party."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11119"
msgstr ""
"They had failed to solve the\n"
"mystery of Sol Sanctum. In doing\n"
"so, they triggered the storm."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11120"
msgstr ""
"Everyone thought that you\n"
"were killed by that boulder,\n"
"{actor_name:5}.{page_break}"
"I can't tell you how glad I was\n"
"to find you were alive!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11121"
msgstr ""
"In fact, nobody was killed\n"
"by the boulder that day!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11122"
msgstr "So that means..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11123"
msgstr ""
"Wait a minute, Kraden...\n"
"Did you just say that {text_effect:2}nobody{reset_text_style}\n"
"was killed by that boulder?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11124"
msgstr ""
"But what about {actor_name:1}'s dad?\n"
"And {actor_name:6} and {actor_name:5}'s parents?\n"
"I thought they'd died that day!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11125"
msgstr "I'm not so sure now..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11126"
msgstr ""
"Yes! If {actor_name:5} survived,\n"
"Kyle and the others may have\n"
"as well..."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11127"
msgstr ""
"Why didn't you tell us? We\n"
"could have worked together to\n"
"save your parents, couldn't we?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11128"
msgstr ""
"Except that we had only just\n"
"begun our journey, and we\n"
"simply weren't strong enough."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11129"
msgstr ""
"He's right. They were too\n"
"powerful then... It would have\n"
"been impossible."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11130"
msgstr ""
"There's more to it than that.\n"
"He had another reason to\n"
"light the lighthouse beacons."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11131"
msgstr ""
"Unless the lighthouse beacons\n"
"are all lit, Weyard will eventually\n"
"be destroyed."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11132"
msgstr ""
"Destroyed?\n"
"But...how? Why?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11133"
msgstr ""
"King Hydros, ruler of Lemuria,\n"
"says that our world is steadily\n"
"shrinking."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11134"
msgstr ""
"Elemental energy drives the\n"
"growth of civilization. Without\n"
"it, we and our world will wither."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11135"
msgstr ""
"All that because the lighthouses\n"
"aren't illuminated?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11136"
msgstr ""
"According to my research,\n"
"that seems to be the case."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11137"
msgstr ""
"But...once the lighthouses\n"
"are all lit, you said the world\n"
"would end anyway!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11138"
msgstr ""
"That...might be true, too... But\n"
"if we do nothing, the world\n"
"will definitely end."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11139"
msgstr ""
"Wait for the end of the world\n"
"to come or wind up accidentally\n"
"triggering it ourselves...{page_break}"
"What a choice..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11140"
msgstr ""
"Nothing is certain. There is\n"
"no way to prevent the world\n"
"from reaching its natural end."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11141"
msgstr ""
"However, we can fight to save\n"
"the world from withering away\n"
"due to the actions of men."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11142"
msgstr ""
"And, {actor_name:5}, you knew this?\n"
"You were helping them because\n"
"you knew what was happening?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11143"
msgstr ""
"You're a lot smarter than\n"
"I remember you being..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11144"
msgstr ""
"You just figured it out along\n"
"the way, huh? That's still\n"
"pretty darned smart."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11145"
msgstr ""
"Why did you wait so long\n"
"to tell me? I would have\n"
"helped you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11146"
msgstr ""
"You wouldn't have done it\n"
"before, {actor_name:1}...{page_break}"
"It would have meant violating\n"
"the sacred teachings of Vale."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11147"
msgstr ""
"Now that we know all of\n"
"this, shouldn't we be going?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11148"
msgstr "Hamma!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11149"
msgstr "Hello again..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11150"
msgstr ""
"Hamma! You...know {actor_name:1}?\n"
"And his companions, too?"

msgctxt "message"
msgid "11151"
msgstr ""
"We met at the temple on the\n"
"edge of the Lamakan Desert..."

msgctxt "message"
msgid "11152"
msgstr ""
"I'm Hamma, descendant\n"
"of the Anemos."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11153"
msgstr ""
"I was born in Contigo, and\n"
"I inherited the power of\n"
"the Anemos."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11154"
msgstr ""
"Hey... We just got into Contigo,\n"
"and we found out this is where\n"
"{actor_name:3} was born!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11155"
msgstr ""
"Yeah... We also learned\n"
"that he's got a sister!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11156"
msgstr "Sister... You don't mean..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11157"
msgstr "That would be me, yes."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11158"
msgstr ""
"Not now, {actor_name:3}...\n"
"This isn't the time."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11159"
msgstr ""
"Three lighthouses have been\n"
"lit... The elements have been\n"
"thrown out of balance."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11160"
msgstr ""
"Jupiter is growing stronger,\n"
"and the north grows colder\n"
"with every passing moment."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11161"
msgstr ""
"You must hurry to Mars\n"
"Lighthouse. Ignite its beacon,\n"
"before all of Weyard freezes..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11162"
msgstr ""
"Mars Lighthouse? Agatio\n"
"has the Mars Star. He's\n"
"on his way to light it now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11163"
msgstr ""
"I doubt they will be able to\n"
"light the Mars beacon..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11164"
msgstr "Why's that?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11165"
msgstr ""
"There is a powerful force\n"
"that does not want to see\n"
"Mars rekindled."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11166"
msgstr ""
"You will fail as well...unless\n"
"you pool your strengths\n"
"together and fight as one."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11167"
msgstr ""
"This is bad.\n"
"We have to go...now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11168"
msgstr ""
"I had hoped that you\n"
"would feel that way..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11169"
msgstr ""
"I've prepared a gift for you,\n"
"to aid you on your way to\n"
"Mars Lighthouse."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11170"
msgstr ""
"I must leave you now, but\n"
"we will meet at the inlet."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11171"
msgstr ""
"I'm sorry we left Venus\n"
"Lighthouse without seeing you...\n"
"I'm sorry for making you worry..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11172"
msgstr ""
"Maybe when this is all over, we\n"
"can all go on a trip together."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11173"
msgstr ""
"Hey, {actor_name:6}, you sure seem\n"
"calm, considering that we're\n"
"racing to meet our enemies..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11174"
msgstr ""
"I'm just relieved that we've\n"
"sorted our differences..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11175"
msgstr ""
"Me too, {actor_name:4}... We could\n"
"not have stood divided\n"
"against a common foe."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11176"
msgstr ""
"Yeah, I guess I'm a little\n"
"happy that we're not going\n"
"to have to beat {actor_name:5} up."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11177"
msgstr ""
"Listen, this is {actor_name:5}'s quest\n"
"now... We're just doing what\n"
"we can to help out..."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11178"
msgstr "Aren't you happy?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11179"
msgstr ""
"Everything's finally come\n"
"together... This is how it was\n"
"meant to be, {actor_name:5}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11180"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry about the future,\n"
"{actor_name:5}... Enjoy this brief\n"
"moment's happiness."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11181"
msgstr ""
"But Hamma's waiting for us.\n"
"Let's go to our ship!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo128"
msgid "11182"
msgstr ""
"You have to hurry! I think\n"
"the ship from the geoglyphs\n"
"is going to take off soon!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo129"
msgid "11183"
msgstr ""
"First, the lighthouse is lit, and\n"
"now, we're going to see a\n"
"flying boat! It's like a festival!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo130"
msgid "11184"
msgstr ""
"The boss said it was all right\n"
"for us to go to the inlet once\n"
"all the customers leave.{page_break}"
"So hurry up and leave,\n"
"so we can go watch\n"
"the boat!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo131"
msgid "11185"
msgstr ""
"They've finished putting the\n"
"wings on the boat, but I don't\n"
"see what the big deal is.{page_break}"
"It's just a flying boat, for\n"
"crying out loud!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo132"
msgid "11186"
msgstr ""
"Once all our customers\n"
"leave, I'm free to go. So\n"
"hurry up already!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo133"
msgid "11187"
msgstr ""
"I can't believe it... All of the\n"
"hopes of the people of Atteka\n"
"have come true here, in Contigo!{page_break}"
"It's like a miracle, a dream\n"
"come true! This calls for\n"
"a festival!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo134"
msgid "11188"
msgstr ""
"All these years, I thought it was\n"
"just a children's story, but now\n"
"it's all coming true..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo135"
msgid "11189"
msgstr ""
"It was kind of impressive\n"
"watching the procession\n"
"carrying those wings, though..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo136"
msgid "11190"
msgstr ""
"A flying ship... Surely, it must\n"
"be a miracle. I'll have to\n"
"study this closely."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo137"
msgid "11191"
msgstr ""
"Perhaps if I see a miracle\n"
"with my own eyes, my faith\n"
"will be restored once more..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgHammaReturnedTo"
msgid "11192"
msgstr ""
"Hamma returned to Contigo\n"
"after all these years... Right\n"
"when we finished the wings!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWasYourBoat"
msgid "11193"
msgstr ""
"Was your boat really the same\n"
"one in the geoglyph? What's\n"
"that all about?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgEveryoneSWaiting"
msgid "11194"
msgstr ""
"Everyone's waiting down by\n"
"the beach.{page_break}"
"They all want to see the boat\n"
"fly with their own eyes."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgAMassiveRock"
msgid "11195"
msgstr ""
"A massive rock blocked the\n"
"entrance to the inlet after the\n"
"lighthouse beacon was lit...{page_break}"
"If that ship's ever going to\n"
"leave the inlet, it's gonna\n"
"have to fly to do it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWhereDoYouThink"
msgid "11196"
msgstr "Where do you think you're going?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11197"
msgstr ""
"We worked really hard\n"
"on that ship of yours!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11198"
msgstr ""
"I want to see our handiwork\n"
"take flight. Don't you, buddy?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11199"
msgstr "I want to!  Boy, do I want to!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11200"
msgstr ""
"So hurry up!\n"
"We want to see the boat fly!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11201"
msgstr "Thanks, buddy!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgTheVillagersAre"
msgid "11202"
msgstr ""
"The villagers are all waiting to\n"
"see the ship fly. So how's about\n"
"getting on with the flying!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgHammaWouldnT"
msgid "11203"
msgstr ""
"Hamma wouldn't let us get\n"
"any closer, so we're waiting\n"
"here to watch the ship leave."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWhenPeopleWork"
msgid "11204"
msgstr ""
"When people work together,\n"
"even a little spiritual power\n"
"can work great wonders.{page_break}"
"We sent everyone back to\n"
"the village so that their hopes\n"
"would not impair your flight."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWeVeBeen"
msgid "11205"
msgstr ""
"We've been working forever\n"
"on getting these wings\n"
"onto the boat!{page_break}"
"We're not used to working like\n"
"this... It's making me dizzy!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWhoBuiltThe"
msgid "11206"
msgstr ""
"Who built the boat from the\n"
"geoglyph, anyway?{page_break}"
"Is there another tribe that's\n"
"descended from the Anemos\n"
"besides our tribe in Contigo?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgHammaIsThe"
msgid "11207"
msgstr ""
"Hamma is the new leader of\n"
"Contigo. She bears the powers\n"
"of the Anemos, after all.{page_break}"
"But I still think she shouldn't\n"
"be ordering us to help fix\n"
"up your boat."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIfThatBoat"
msgid "11208"
msgstr ""
"If that boat's gonna get out\n"
"of the inlet, it's gonna have\n"
"to fly. I want to see that."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgItSAmazing"
msgid "11209"
msgstr ""
"It's amazing to think that my\n"
"hard work is going to help\n"
"make that boat fly."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgHammaSaysThat"
msgid "11210"
msgstr ""
"Hamma says that our own\n"
"hopes and dreams might\n"
"prevent the boat from flying.{page_break}"
"It's as though, by wanting it\n"
"too much, we'll actually\n"
"prevent it from happening."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWeCanT"
msgid "11211"
msgstr ""
"We can't get too close to\n"
"the boat, or it might not fly...{page_break}"
"We've just got to have\n"
"everyone watch from afar."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgItSAlmost"
msgid "11212"
msgstr ""
"It's almost time... Time to\n"
"watch a legend become reality!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIfEveryoneWill"
msgid "11213"
msgstr ""
"If everyone will just obey\n"
"Hamma's request, the ship\n"
"will surely fly."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWhenTheWinged"
msgid "11214"
msgstr ""
"When the winged ship of Anemos\n"
"flies once again, the whole land\n"
"shall be made free...{page_break}"
"That's what the legend says,\n"
"anyway... But what land needs\n"
"freeing? We seem free enough..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgOnceYouRemove"
msgid "11215"
msgstr ""
"Once you remove the stone\n"
"anchors weighing the ship\n"
"down, it should fly..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgTheDayHas"
msgid "11216"
msgstr ""
"The day has finally come that\n"
"the ship will fly on the Wings\n"
"of Anemos..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgTheAnemosWere"
msgid "11217"
msgstr ""
"The Anemos were powerful,\n"
"sure, but can their power really\n"
"make a great ship fly?{page_break}"
"No... No, I must not doubt...\n"
"I must have faith that it will\n"
"fly. It is meant to be."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgTheseWarriorsWill"
msgid "11218"
msgstr ""
"These warriors will know what\n"
"to do... They'll know how to\n"
"save the land..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIHearThatThe"
msgid "11219"
msgstr ""
"I hear that the warriors brought\n"
"the Hover Jade back with them...{page_break}"
"Now, that's something that I'd\n"
"really like to see."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIVeBeenWaiting"
msgid "11220"
msgstr ""
"I've been waiting for you,\n"
"{actor_name:5}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11221"
msgstr "Take a look at your ship."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11222"
msgstr ""
"Now that you have been given\n"
"wings, all obstacles in your\n"
"path will vanish forever..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11223"
msgstr ""
"However, it is not the wings\n"
"alone that grant your ship\n"
"the power of flight."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11224"
msgstr ""
"Psynergy is the force that\n"
"powers the Wings of Anemos."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11225"
msgstr ""
"If the ship is to fly, you\n"
"will need to focus the\n"
"power of your minds..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11226"
msgstr ""
"You have visited Shaman\n"
"Village recently, have you not?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11227"
msgstr ""
"Now is the time to make\n"
"use of the powers you\n"
"acquired there."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11228"
msgstr ""
"Now... Use the power of\n"
"Hover to raise your ship!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11229"
msgstr ""
"At first, you may not want to\n"
"move your ship too high or\n"
"too far..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11230"
msgstr ""
"It will be difficult at first, but\n"
"that is to be expected... After\n"
"all, this is your first flight."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11231"
msgstr ""
"But your quest should not\n"
"demand much more of you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11232"
msgstr ""
"Now, be confident\n"
"and set sail!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11233"
msgstr ""
"All of Contigo is watching...\n"
"Show them your power, and\n"
"make your vessel fly!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgUseYourPsynergy"
msgid "11234"
msgstr ""
"Use your Psynergy to raise\n"
"your ship and fly over reefs."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgTravelSafelyThe"
msgid "11235"
msgstr ""
"Travel safely, {actor_name:3}...\n"
"The world depends on you."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo138"
msgid "11236"
msgstr ""
"I got stuck doing chores at\n"
"home, and I had to miss\n"
"watching the ship take off."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo139"
msgid "11237"
msgstr ""
"Everyone's been going on\n"
"about how amazing it was\n"
"to watch the ship fly...{page_break}"
"I wish I could have been\n"
"there to see it. I guess it\n"
"was pretty moving."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo140"
msgid "11238"
msgstr ""
"It must be so exciting to\n"
"travel around the world\n"
"in a flying ship."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo141"
msgid "11239"
msgstr ""
"Hamma was telling us that the\n"
"world is a dangerous place.\n"
"I wonder what she meant.{page_break}"
"I think she's concerned about\n"
"the elemental balance..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo142"
msgid "11240"
msgstr ""
"I saw the ship fly!\n"
"Now I want to see what it\n"
"looks like from on board!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo143"
msgid "11241"
msgstr ""
"It wasn't what I expected,\n"
"but seeing the ship take\n"
"off was still amazing."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo144"
msgid "11242"
msgstr ""
"I didn't get to see the ship\n"
"take off, but I'm not really\n"
"all that disappointed.{page_break}"
"I heard that it wasn't\n"
"that impressive anyway."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo145"
msgid "11243"
msgstr ""
"Some people were talking\n"
"about how the ship wasn't\n"
"really that impressive.{page_break}"
"Why would they say that?\n"
"A ship actually flew\n"
"through the air!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo146"
msgid "11244"
msgstr ""
"I couldn't fly in the air,\n"
"that's for sure. I get motion\n"
"sickness just walking around."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo147"
msgid "11245"
msgstr ""
"I heard that the world could\n"
"freeze over soon... I hope\n"
"{actor_name:3} does what he needs to."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo148"
msgid "11246"
msgstr ""
"The ship looked like it\n"
"had a few problems trying\n"
"to get off the ground.{page_break}"
"I guess it was because\n"
"the crew had never made\n"
"a ship fly before."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo149"
msgid "11247"
msgstr ""
"All of those legends did\n"
"nothing but build up people's\n"
"expectations.{page_break}"
"I'm just glad to know that\n"
"the ship flew at all..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo150"
msgid "11248"
msgstr ""
"I guess the lighthouse was\n"
"lit because {actor_name:3} and Hamma\n"
"finally returned to Contigo."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo151"
msgid "11249"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:3} doesn't remember\n"
"his mother, because he was\n"
"taken away at such an early age.{page_break}"
"But I saw her eyes the day he\n"
"went away. Tears welled up,\n"
"and she couldn't stop crying."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo152"
msgid "11250"
msgstr ""
"From the look on {actor_name:3}'s\n"
"face, whatever happened at the\n"
"lighthouse must have been bad."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo153"
msgid "11251"
msgstr ""
"Hamma will stay with us, but\n"
"{actor_name:3} is leaving again.{page_break}"
"The power of Anemos must\n"
"be a terrible responsibility\n"
"for such a young boy."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo154"
msgid "11252"
msgstr ""
"I wonder how {actor_name:3} feels\n"
"now that he knows what\n"
"happened to his mother.{page_break}"
"Hamma seems so closed up...\n"
"I wonder if she'll talk to him\n"
"about it..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo155"
msgid "11253"
msgstr ""
"Someday, I'm gonna fight {actor_name:3},\n"
"and then I'll be the legendary\n"
"hero of Contigo!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo156"
msgid "11254"
msgstr ""
"{text_effect:4}Brrr...Brrr... It's been really\n"
"cold since the lighthouse\n"
"beacon was lit!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo157"
msgid "11255"
msgstr ""
"Winter just ended, but\n"
"it keeps getting colder.\n"
"What's going on?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo158"
msgid "11256"
msgstr ""
"Jupiter Lighthouse has been\n"
"called the beacon of wind... Is\n"
"that why it's so windy and cold?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo159"
msgid "11257"
msgstr ""
"Hamma says that if {actor_name:3}\n"
"fails, it will continue to get\n"
"colder and colder."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo160"
msgid "11258"
msgstr ""
"The lighthouse has been lit,\n"
"and we've made a ship fly...\n"
"Our legends are coming to life!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo161"
msgid "11259"
msgstr ""
"It's up to the people of\n"
"Contigo to live up to\n"
"our own legends."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo162"
msgid "11260"
msgstr ""
"Mom and Dad have been\n"
"walking around in a daze\n"
"since the ship took off."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo163"
msgid "11261"
msgstr ""
"The baby's forehead is\n"
"furrowed, like it's thinking."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo164"
msgid "11262"
msgstr "Goo goo. Gaa gaa... Waaa!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11263"
msgstr ""
"Drafts! I hate drafts! This\n"
"stupid house is always cold!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11264"
msgstr ""
"Now that we've finished the\n"
"wings, we should fix the house."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo165"
msgid "11265"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:3} has the power of\n"
"prophecy, but I'll bet he didn't\n"
"see this coming!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo166"
msgid "11266"
msgstr ""
"Now that I think about it,\n"
"this very day will probably\n"
"become a legend, too!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo167"
msgid "11267"
msgstr ""
"It's time to fix those drafts\n"
"now that the wings are done!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo168"
msgid "11268"
msgstr ""
"Goo... It's getting colder...\n"
"Gagoo... I want a blanket..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgReturnedToMyNewHome"
msgid "11269"
msgstr ""
"Ah, you've returned! What\n"
"brings you to my new home?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11270"
msgstr "Hamma..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11271"
msgstr ""
"You're my sister... Why didn't\n"
"you tell me sooner? Why didn't\n"
"you tell me when we first met?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11272"
msgstr ""
"You play an important role in\n"
"all this. If I'd told you, you\n"
"would have come here too soon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11273"
msgstr ""
"This place is so familiar...\n"
"I feel like I've lived here\n"
"my whole life."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11274"
msgstr "Look at me, {actor_name:3}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11275"
msgstr ""
"You're too sentimental.{page_break}"
"You would have given up your\n"
"quest to find your true home,\n"
"and we would all now be lost."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11276"
msgstr "What are you saying, sister?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11277"
msgstr ""
"No, not sister... Do not think of\n"
"me as your sister until you\n"
"have fulfilled your destiny."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11278"
msgstr "W-Why?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11279"
msgstr ""
"Our world is falling\n"
"into ruin..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11280"
msgstr ""
"What? Hamma, what do you\n"
"mean? What's happening?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11281"
msgstr ""
"Look, I don't want to interrupt\n"
"your reunion or anything, but..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11282"
msgstr ""
"I couldn't help overhearing\n"
"you say something about the\n"
"world falling apart. What's up?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11283"
msgstr ""
"Our world requires a delicate\n"
"balance of elemental forces.\n"
"That balance has been disturbed."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11284"
msgstr ""
"Without that balance, one\n"
"element might be lost beneath\n"
"the others, straining Weyard."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11285"
msgstr ""
"You're talking about\n"
"Mars Lighthouse, right?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11286"
msgstr ""
"Isn't Agatio taking care of\n"
"Mars Lighthouse? Everything\n"
"should be fine soon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11287"
msgstr ""
"Agatio will not light\n"
"Mars Lighthouse."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11288"
msgstr "You don't think he can do it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11289"
msgstr ""
"No. A great power stands\n"
"ready to oppose them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11290"
msgstr ""
"They lack the power to\n"
"resist that force, and they\n"
"will fall before it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11291"
msgstr ""
"But what will happen if\n"
"Mars Lighthouse isn't lit\n"
"quickly enough?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11292"
msgstr ""
"Our world will be plunged\n"
"into ice."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11293"
msgstr ""
"But what would make\n"
"that happen?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11294"
msgstr ""
"Even I do not know the\n"
"answer to that question."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11295"
msgstr ""
"Ah... Yes, given the way that\n"
"the elements interact, I see..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11296"
msgstr "Kraden, you understand?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11297"
msgstr ""
"Well, I'm only guessing...\n"
"But I think it's a good guess."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11298"
msgstr ""
"Quit fooling around and\n"
"tell me!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11299"
msgstr ""
"The earth is nurturing and\n"
"warm. Many creatures are\n"
"reared in this warmth, you see?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11300"
msgstr "I follow you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11301"
msgstr ""
"It's OK, {actor_name:5}... I don't\n"
"really get it either, but let's\n"
"see where he's taking this..."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11302"
msgstr ""
"Now, think about the ocean.\n"
"It is a cold place, is it not?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11303"
msgstr "Yeah, it is awfully cold..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11304"
msgstr ""
"I don't know what point he's\n"
"trying to make, but I have to\n"
"agree that the ocean's cold..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11305"
msgstr ""
"Both lighthouses were lit,\n"
"and a balance was reached."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11306"
msgstr ""
"But with only the lighthouse\n"
"of wind lit, the balance has\n"
"been disturbed."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11307"
msgstr ""
"I get it... Wind cools things down,\n"
"but it can't heat them up..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11308"
msgstr ""
"When you burn your hand on\n"
"something hot, you blow on\n"
"it to cool it off, don't you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11309"
msgstr ""
"Right, yeah... I've always done\n"
"that without thinking about\n"
"it, but it makes sense, huh?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11310"
msgstr ""
"When Mercury Lighthouse was\n"
"lit, this didn't happen, though.\n"
"I wonder why..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11311"
msgstr ""
"Water cannot cool things\n"
"as swiftly as wind, perhaps."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11312"
msgstr ""
"Or maybe the combined power\n"
"of water and wind is cooling\n"
"things down even faster..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11313"
msgstr ""
"If what Hamma's saying is\n"
"true, we'd better get moving\n"
"again, {actor_name:5}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11314"
msgstr ""
"I got too worked up about\n"
"seeing my sister... Sorry."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11315"
msgstr ""
"It's all right. I'm happy that\n"
"you cared so much..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11316"
msgstr ""
"All right, {actor_name:5}! Let's head\n"
"to Mars Lighthouse!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo170"
msgid "11317"
msgstr ""
"No matter what happens, you\n"
"must light the beacon on\n"
"Mars Lighthouse!{page_break}"
"I hope for your safe return."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo171"
msgid "11318"
msgstr ""
"My heart is with you always,\n"
"{actor_name:3}. Never forget that."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo172"
msgid "11319"
msgstr ""
"A cannon? Yeah, I think I heard\n"
"something about a town up in\n"
"western Angara having one...{page_break}"
"A shot fired from that cannon\n"
"can apparently break even the\n"
"biggest blocks of ice."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo173"
msgid "11320"
msgstr ""
"I'd sure like to see the cannon\n"
"someday. It sounds like a\n"
"powerful weapon..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo174"
msgid "11321"
msgstr ""
"Now that the wings are finished,\n"
"I doubt anyone will be buying\n"
"any more armor from me."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo175"
msgid "11322"
msgstr ""
"Well, if there aren't going to be\n"
"any customers for a while, maybe\n"
"I'll finally take that vacation."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo176"
msgid "11323"
msgstr ""
"It's always such a letdown when\n"
"you finish off a major task like\n"
"fulfilling an ancient prophecy."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo177"
msgid "11324"
msgstr ""
"Now that the wings are done,\n"
"everyone who came to help out\n"
"has left the village... "

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo178"
msgid "11325"
msgstr ""
"All of our work and all of our\n"
"celebration are finally at an end.{page_break}"
"I think Contigo is going to go\n"
"back to being a very quiet place."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo179"
msgid "11326"
msgstr ""
"The inn has become so lonely\n"
"now that everyone's gone\n"
"home.{page_break}"
"We should have an annual\n"
"festival in Contigo to\n"
"commemorate this day!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo180"
msgid "11327"
msgstr ""
"Gosh... We were so busy,\n"
"and now we're totally empty.\n"
"I don't know what to do!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo181"
msgid "11328"
msgstr ""
"Now's my chance to experiment\n"
"with some exciting new dishes!\n"
"What should I make first..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo182"
msgid "11329"
msgstr ""
"It's going to be a little slow\n"
"for a while, but I can't really\n"
"complain, now, can I?{page_break}"
"After all, I saw the lighthouse\n"
"shining again, and I actually\n"
"saw a flying ship!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo183"
msgid "11330"
msgstr ""
"The inn is bound to be slow\n"
"for a little while, but business\n"
"will pick up again.{page_break}"
"Everyone who witnessed the\n"
"events of the past few days\n"
"will want to come back."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo184"
msgid "11331"
msgstr ""
"What are we going to do?\n"
"All the excitement is over,\n"
"and I'm going to be bored!{page_break}"
"I was starting to like all the\n"
"attention I was getting!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo185"
msgid "11332"
msgstr ""
"Seeing that ship take flight\n"
"was the most moving thing\n"
"I've ever seen...{page_break}"
"I think I'll have to preserve\n"
"it for future generations...\n"
"in cake form!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo186"
msgid "11333"
msgstr ""
"It was a miracle that made\n"
"all of the legends of the\n"
"Anemos come true...{page_break}"
"I'm not entirely sure,\n"
"but I think my faith\n"
"has been restored!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo187"
msgid "11334"
msgstr ""
"It was a shock to see\n"
"such a huge ship float.{page_break}"
"It made me realize how\n"
"small we all truly are."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo188"
msgid "11335"
msgstr ""
"I can't believe that a ship\n"
"just like the one in the\n"
"geoglyph actually exists.{page_break}"
"And I think everyone's proud\n"
"to have helped to make the\n"
"legends come true!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo189"
msgid "11336"
msgstr ""
"That flying ship looked so\n"
"fake... It didn't look anything\n"
"like I'd imagined it would.{page_break}"
"Nobody else was complaining,\n"
"but they don't pay attention\n"
"to the details, like I do."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo190"
msgid "11337"
msgstr ""
"Look closely at the\n"
"geoglyph. Study it,\n"
"examine its details...{page_break}"
"The more you stare at it,\n"
"the more you recognize the\n"
"greatness of the Anemos."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo191"
msgid "11338"
msgstr ""
"I'm convinced there's something\n"
"hidden in the Sanctum.{page_break}"
"I just know it says something\n"
"about it on the wall."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo192"
msgid "11339"
msgstr ""
"All the amazing things we've\n"
"seen and done, all the legends\n"
"that have come true...{page_break}"
"And I still can't get into\n"
"the secret chambers of\n"
"the Anemos Sanctum!!!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo193"
msgid "11340"
msgstr ""
"He's an odd boy, but I'm glad\n"
"that {actor_name:3} has returned\n"
"to Contigo at last..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo194"
msgid "11341"
msgstr ""
"We all came together and\n"
"worked to make the legends\n"
"come true...{page_break}"
"It's really inspiring... Actually,\n"
"it gives me goosebumps...\n"
"{text_effect:4}Brrrr...{reset_text_style}"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo195"
msgid "11342"
msgstr ""
"All right, so we've followed\n"
"the instructions on the wall,\n"
"and we {text_effect:2}still{reset_text_style} can't get in!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo196"
msgid "11343"
msgstr ""
"If you tap on the floor or\n"
"walls, you can hear a hollow\n"
"sort of sound.{page_break}"
"I'm convinced that there's\n"
"nothing on the other side!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo197"
msgid "11344"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:3} was supposed to be\n"
"a great, manly hero... I guess not\n"
"all the legends came true..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIVeBeenWatching"
msgid "11345"
msgstr ""
"I've been watching the skies,\n"
"hoping I could catch another\n"
"glimpse of the flying ship."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIWonderWhat"
msgid "11346"
msgstr ""
"I wonder what's on the other\n"
"side of the ocean... I should be\n"
"happy where I am, but...{page_break}"
"Whenever I think about that\n"
"flying ship, I want to leave\n"
"home, to explore the world!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgAllOfOur"
msgid "11347"
msgstr ""
"All of our myths and legends\n"
"have taught us that the sea\n"
"is a dangerous, fearsome power.{page_break}"
"But on the day the ship\n"
"left, the sea was so calm\n"
"and romantic looking..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgYouReGoingNorth"
msgid "11348"
msgstr ""
"You're going north? I hear it's\n"
"always winter in the lands\n"
"to the north, so bundle up!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWheneverILook"
msgid "11349"
msgstr ""
"Whenever I look at the sky,\n"
"I think about that flying ship,\n"
"and I want to travel the world."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIWishI"
msgid "11350"
msgstr ""
"I wish I could travel to the\n"
"end of the sea on that\n"
"beautiful flying ship."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgEveryoneInContigo"
msgid "11351"
msgstr ""
"Everyone in Contigo used\n"
"to be afraid of the ocean.{page_break}"
"But now, everyone who saw the\n"
"ship take off sees the sea\n"
"filled with wonder and romance."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIVeDecided"
msgid "11352"
msgstr ""
"I've decided to become...\n"
"an adventurer!{page_break}"
"One day, when {actor_name:3} and his\n"
"companions return, I will join\n"
"them on their amazing ship!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo198"
msgid "11353"
msgstr ""
"The legends tell us that a\n"
"great calamity brought an\n"
"end to the Anemos...{page_break}"
"It had something to do with\n"
"the light from the lighthouses\n"
"being extinguished."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo199"
msgid "11354"
msgstr ""
"That crater behind the village\n"
"is supposed to be where the\n"
"city of the Anemos was.{page_break}"
"The legend says that, one day,\n"
"it just lifted off the ground and\n"
"flew away!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo200"
msgid "11355"
msgstr ""
"The ancient city of the Anemos\n"
"was located right near the ruins.{page_break}"
"That crater nearby is where\n"
"the city once was."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo201"
msgid "11356"
msgstr ""
"Cities flying up into the\n"
"sky? I don't buy that for\n"
"a second!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo202"
msgid "11357"
msgstr ""
"If a ship can rise up from\n"
"the sea, why can't a city\n"
"rise up from the ground?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo203"
msgid "11358"
msgstr ""
"I've seen a lot of weird\n"
"things lately... Maybe I ought\n"
"to listen to those legends."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo204"
msgid "11359"
msgstr ""
"The city of the Anemos rose up\n"
"into the sky and became what\n"
"we now call the Moon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgContigo205"
msgid "11360"
msgstr ""
"Wait... The city of Anemos\n"
"flew up into the sky?{page_break}"
"All right, that's just stupid!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWeDidIt"
msgid "11361"
msgstr ""
"We did it! The ship took\n"
"off without a hitch!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11362"
msgstr ""
"Yeah, but...shouldn't it be\n"
"flying a little higher than this?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11363"
msgstr ""
"Hamma told us that we wouldn't\n"
"be able to fly very high until we\n"
"were more familiar with Hover."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11364"
msgstr ""
"Let's see how far we\n"
"can take this thing!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11365"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:7}, what's wrong? You\n"
"don't look happy..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11366"
msgstr ""
"Do you remember on Idejima,\n"
"when I told you I had my own\n"
"reasons for joining your quest?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11367"
msgstr ""
"You were so secretive!\n"
"Are you going to tell us now?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11368"
msgstr "... ..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11369"
msgstr ""
"You've gone quiet again...{pause_20_skippable}\n"
"It's OK... You don't have to\n"
"tell us if you're not ready yet."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11370"
msgstr ""
"I thought that if I went to\n"
"Jupiter Lighthouse, I would\n"
"learn who I was..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11371"
msgstr ""
"I remember the people of\n"
"Lalivero talking about how\n"
"{actor_name:7} fell from the sky..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11372"
msgstr ""
"All my life, I've been looking\n"
"for the answer... Where was I\n"
"born, and why was I abandoned?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11373"
msgstr ""
"You knew {actor_name:5} was going to\n"
"Jupiter Lighthouse eventually,\n"
"and so you went along with him."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11374"
msgstr ""
"But you didn't find any answers,\n"
"did you, {actor_name:7}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11375"
msgstr ""
"I'm sorry, {actor_name:7}... I was so\n"
"excited to find Contigo that I\n"
"didn't consider your feelings."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11376"
msgstr ""
"What? Why is everyone so\n"
"down all of a sudden?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11377"
msgstr "... ..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11378"
msgstr ""
"Faran raised {actor_name:7} like his own\n"
"daughter. He's cared for her\n"
"ever since he first found her!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11379"
msgstr "Yes, that's true, but..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11380"
msgstr ""
"But you can never be his\n"
"real daughter, is that it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11381"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:2}! You don't have to\n"
"be so blunt about it!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11382"
msgstr ""
"No, he's right... I'd want to know\n"
"my real parents, no matter how\n"
"caring Faran might have been."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11383"
msgstr ""
"You think so? If it were me, I\n"
"doubt it'd bother me at all..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11384"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:7}, you may not know this,\n"
"but you and I are very similar..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11385"
msgstr "What do you mean?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11386"
msgstr ""
"Well, it's not exactly the\n"
"same situation, but..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11387"
msgstr ""
"I was born in a poor village. My\n"
"memories are hazy, but I still\n"
"remember it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11388"
msgstr ""
"I was only four when Babi\n"
"took me under his wing."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11389"
msgstr ""
"You see, even though I was\n"
"young, I was quite intelligent.\n"
"Babi had heard about me..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11390"
msgstr ""
"And Babi took you to Tolbi\n"
"to further your education, to\n"
"raise you as a scholar..."

msgctxt "message"
msgid "11391"
msgstr ""
"I was separated from my parents\n"
"so early in life... I've never known\n"
"the comforts of a true home.{end_wait} "

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11392"
msgstr ""
"Faran has always been like\n"
"a father to me... I must have\n"
"been very lucky."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11393"
msgstr "I should say so."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11394"
msgstr ""
"Thank you, Kraden...\n"
"I feel better now..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11395"
msgstr "I'm glad I could help."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11396"
msgstr ""
"Well, we should be going...\n"
"Let's hurry on, {actor_name:5}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgHeyWait2"
msgid "11397"
msgstr "Hey, wait!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11398"
msgstr ""
"Master Hammet requested that\n"
"I deliver this to {actor_name:1}, and\n"
"I totally forgot about it!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11399"
msgstr "Well, you'd better hurry."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11400"
msgstr ""
"I'm supposed to deliver this\n"
"to {actor_name:1}... It's not too late, is it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11401"
msgstr ""
"On my way here, I stopped in\n"
"Kalay briefly to speak with\n"
"Master Hammet."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11402"
msgstr ""
"He was quite upset that you\n"
"hadn't returned to visit him\n"
"so that he could thank you."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11403"
msgstr ""
"So he requested that I take\n"
"this with me to Atteka."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11404"
msgstr ""
"It is a gift of thanks from\n"
"Master Hammet. Take it, please."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho01"
msgid "11405"
msgstr ""
"Welcome to Loho! We've been\n"
"excavating all sorts of ores\n"
"to get the metals inside!{page_break}"
"The metal used to make the\n"
"ancient ruins might have come\n"
"from these very rocks!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho02"
msgid "11406"
msgstr ""
"We have a lot of important\n"
"excavations going on, but\n"
"we're also doing some mining."

msgctxt "MsgLoho03"
msgid "11407"
msgstr ""
"Some of the miners found an\n"
"ancient cannon when they\n"
"were digging a while back.{page_break}"
"If you want to see it, it's\n"
"over by the wall near the\n"
"ruins.{end_wait} "

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho04"
msgid "11408"
msgstr ""
"That wall seems indestructible!\n"
"We've been trying to dig\n"
"through it for a while now.{page_break}"
"We're pretty sure there are\n"
"some valuable metals and\n"
"minerals on the other side."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho05"
msgid "11409"
msgstr ""
"We only settled here a short\n"
"while ago, and we found all\n"
"those ruins here...{page_break}"
"We named our settlement\n"
"Loho, but I've been wondering\n"
"what it used to be called..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho06"
msgid "11410"
msgstr ""
"Everyone in Loho sure loves\n"
"digging. It's not all mining...\n"
"We're interested in history, too."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho07"
msgid "11411"
msgstr ""
"All we need is a way to use\n"
"the cannon to knock down the\n"
"wall... That would be great.{page_break}"
"Then, we could get rid of the\n"
"cannon altogether. We don't\n"
"have any use for weapons here."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho08"
msgid "11412"
msgstr ""
"If we can't get through that\n"
"wall, we'll never know what's\n"
"on the other side..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho09"
msgid "11413"
msgstr ""
"Once we can get through the\n"
"wall, there will be enough\n"
"work for everyone in town!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho10"
msgid "11414"
msgstr ""
"If you want to be a miner,\n"
"you have to know the earth...\n"
"You have to know where to dig."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho11"
msgid "11415"
msgstr ""
"This is the spot. A good hole\n"
"here, and you'll dig up some\n"
"fantastic ore..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho12"
msgid "11416"
msgstr ""
"I haven't found anything worth\n"
"the trouble of digging up. It's\n"
"time to find another spot."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho13"
msgid "11417"
msgstr ""
"If you live in Loho and you\n"
"don't dig, you're not one of\n"
"us... You don't belong."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho14"
msgid "11418"
msgstr ""
"Real experts can find the best\n"
"spots to dig in a single glance."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho15"
msgid "11419"
msgstr ""
"Once you've been mining for\n"
"a while, it's like the ground says\n"
"to you, \"Hey! Hey, you! Dig here!\""

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho16"
msgid "11420"
msgstr ""
"I think I'm starting to lose\n"
"my touch... None of my digs\n"
"has produced anything at all."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho17"
msgid "11421"
msgstr ""
"Commerce really took off\n"
"when we started this mining\n"
"colony in Loho.{page_break}"
"You just have to know how\n"
"to make the most out of\n"
"what's around you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho18"
msgid "11422"
msgstr ""
"Whenever someone strikes\n"
"gold, we get a rush of visitors,\n"
"and business just takes off."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho19"
msgid "11423"
msgstr ""
"If you're only here for\n"
"the cannon, you can\n"
"forget about it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho20"
msgid "11424"
msgstr ""
"If the cannon is truly as\n"
"powerful as the people say,\n"
"we can't just give it away."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho21"
msgid "11425"
msgstr ""
"We brought the cannon up here\n"
"to break down the old wall, but\n"
"we don't have any ammunition..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho22"
msgid "11426"
msgstr ""
"You can put metal balls in\n"
"the barrel, but what makes\n"
"them come out again?{page_break}"
"It looks a little like an old\n"
"ballista, but the way it works\n"
"is totally different."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "MsgLoho23"
msgid "11427"
msgstr "Did you want this cannon?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11428"
msgstr ""
"Well, if you can figure out\n"
"a way to break down this\n"
"wall, it's all yours."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11429"
msgstr ""
"All we really want to do is\n"
"break down that wall right\n"
"there...{page_break}"
"If we can find someone to do\n"
"that, we'll give 'im the cannon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho24"
msgid "11430"
msgstr ""
"Cannons are so heavy! Why did\n"
"we bring it up here if we're not\n"
"going to use it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho25"
msgid "11431"
msgstr ""
"What idiot said that we'd be\n"
"able to destroy that wall if\n"
"we dragged the cannon up here?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho26"
msgid "11432"
msgstr ""
"All right, we figured out that\n"
"you need to put a steel ball in\n"
"there, but what do you do then?{page_break}"
"You can stick a ball in there\n"
"just fine, but I don't think it'll\n"
"be coming out on its own..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho27"
msgid "11433"
msgstr "It looks like it's empty."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11434"
msgstr ""
"This can't be used as\n"
"a cannonball."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho28"
msgid "11435"
msgstr "Is everyone all right?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11436"
msgstr ""
"Did you hear that? That\n"
"sound was incredible!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11437"
msgstr ""
"What do you think you're\n"
"doing, making all that noise?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11438"
msgstr "Hey, look at that!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11439"
msgstr ""
"What are you looking at?\n"
"It wasn't me! It was the wall!\n"
"Look at the wall!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11440"
msgstr "The wall... It's gone!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11441"
msgstr ""
"Well, it's mostly gone, yeah...\n"
"You can get through to the\n"
"other side now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11442"
msgstr ""
"How did you manage to\n"
"break down the wall?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11443"
msgstr ""
"Ah, never mind... What's important\n"
"here is that we can dig on\n"
"the other side of the wall now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11444"
msgstr ""
"Yeah, who cares how it\n"
"happened? We can dig again!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11445"
msgstr ""
"Well, you did what we asked,\n"
"so the cannon's all yours!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11446"
msgstr ""
"Hmmm... It's gonna be tough\n"
"carrying that thing around..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11447"
msgstr ""
"Those guys are new in town, aren't\n"
"they? Do you think they came\n"
"from Atteka or Hesperia?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11448"
msgstr ""
"I don't know, but I can tell\n"
"you they came by boat..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11449"
msgstr ""
"Yeah, I saw one anchored\n"
"off the beach!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11450"
msgstr "That boat's yours, isn't it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11451"
msgstr ""
"Well, why don't you let us\n"
"get that cannon onto your\n"
"boat for you, hm?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11452"
msgstr ""
"Look, the only way to get\n"
"here is by boat, and I see\n"
"a boat right there!{page_break}"
"Don't tell me it's not yours!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11453"
msgstr ""
"I don't know why I'm offering,\n"
"but why don't you let us put\n"
"it aboard your boat for you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho29"
msgid "11454"
msgstr ""
"Was that you that fired\n"
"the cannon earlier?{page_break}"
"If you know how to use\n"
"the cannon, you'll be able\n"
"to sail in the Northern Sea."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho30"
msgid "11455"
msgstr ""
"That cannon sure gives off\n"
"a serious bang! Everyone in\n"
"Loho was totally shocked!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho31"
msgid "11456"
msgstr ""
"When we found that cannon\n"
"at the dig, I thought it was\n"
"just useless junk.{page_break}"
"If you know how to use\n"
"it, it can be a pretty\n"
"potent tool!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho32"
msgid "11457"
msgstr ""
"Now that the wall's been\n"
"breached, we can get on\n"
"with the mining! Good work!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho33"
msgid "11458"
msgstr ""
"That cannon can shatter any\n"
"of the ice floes that keep the\n"
"ships from trying to sail north."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho34"
msgid "11459"
msgstr ""
"That cannon was really\n"
"loud... Imagine if you were\n"
"standing right next to it!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho35"
msgid "11460"
msgstr ""
"I don't think we should have\n"
"given the cannon away. We\n"
"should have sold it to Tolbi."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho36"
msgid "11461"
msgstr ""
"We don't have anything to worry\n"
"about, now that we can start\n"
"mining in the ruins..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho37"
msgid "11462"
msgstr ""
"I've gotta go stake myself\n"
"a claim on the other side\n"
"of the wall!{page_break}"
"We've found some valuable\n"
"metals out here; think what\n"
"we'll find inside!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho38"
msgid "11463"
msgstr ""
"You probably only want the\n"
"cannon so that you can force\n"
"other people to obey your will."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho39"
msgid "11464"
msgstr ""
"Ah, so you have a quest to\n"
"fulfill, do you? I guess that\n"
"means you're leaving soon.{page_break}"
"When I was your age,\n"
"I used to love the life\n"
"of danger and adventure."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho40"
msgid "11465"
msgstr ""
"I think we've dug up all\n"
"that there is out here.{page_break}"
"I'm going to find myself\n"
"a new spot inside the wall."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho41"
msgid "11466"
msgstr ""
"Thanks for opening up\n"
"the wall... There are some\n"
"great places to dig out here!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho42"
msgid "11467"
msgstr ""
"I keep digging up little, tiny\n"
"gems and metals... But when I\n"
"get enough, I'll be rich!{page_break}"
"After all, when you pile up\n"
"enough dirt, you eventually\n"
"make a mighty mountain!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho43"
msgid "11468"
msgstr ""
"Ha ha ha! I've got this giddy\n"
"feeling, like I'm going to dig\n"
"up a mountain of money!{page_break}"
"Whenever I get this feeling,\n"
"I always dig out a fortune!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho44"
msgid "11469"
msgstr ""
"I just need to stick to this\n"
"one spot. Eventually, I'll\n"
"dig up something valuable!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho45"
msgid "11470"
msgstr ""
"These guys must be really\n"
"busy, sailing around all over\n"
"the world like that."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho46"
msgid "11471"
msgstr ""
"When they get wherever they're\n"
"going, they'll tell the world\n"
"that Loho's got the best metal!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho47"
msgid "11472"
msgstr ""
"Even at my age, I just\n"
"love the feel of digging\n"
"into the earth.{page_break}"
"Still, when you're not digging\n"
"up anything good, you start\n"
"to feel a little frustrated."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho48"
msgid "11473"
msgstr ""
"I only just started digging,\n"
"and I'm already wealthy\n"
"beyond my wildest dreams!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho49"
msgid "11474"
msgstr ""
"I've hit the mother lode!\n"
"I keep on digging, and I\n"
"keep getting more and more!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho50"
msgid "11475"
msgstr ""
"It doesn't matter how old\n"
"you get... Nothing beats the\n"
"feeling of digging a new mine."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho51"
msgid "11476"
msgstr ""
"I hear you took our cannon\n"
"in exchange for knocking\n"
"down that ancient wall.{page_break}"
"I'll be sorry to see it go...\n"
"That cannon was going\n"
"to make Loho famous."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho52"
msgid "11477"
msgstr ""
"Now, we don't have a symbol\n"
"anymore... We just have a\n"
"town full of holes."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho53"
msgid "11478"
msgstr ""
"You've acquired a splendid\n"
"cannon. Just be sure that\n"
"you use it wisely."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho54"
msgid "11479"
msgstr ""
"It worries me to no end,\n"
"thinking of the evils one\n"
"could do with that cannon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgYouDonT"
msgid "11480"
msgstr ""
"You don't have anything to\n"
"worry about. We got the cannon\n"
"onto your ship with no problems."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11481"
msgstr ""
"Now, we're going to start\n"
"excavating the ground north of\n"
"the wall you knocked a hole in."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho55"
msgid "11482"
msgstr ""
"I saw some of the village\n"
"men carrying the cannon\n"
"out of town..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho56"
msgid "11483"
msgstr ""
"I don't know where they were\n"
"taking it, but I'm glad the\n"
"cannon's gone...{page_break}"
"I think they just wanted to\n"
"make some room for us to\n"
"begin mining again."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgLoho57"
msgid "11484"
msgstr ""
"{protagonist_name} checked the sign{page_break}"
"It reads \"People staying at\n"
"the inn can check in at the\n"
"counter."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx01"
msgid "11485"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}! Welcome back to\n"
"Prox! It looks like only Mars\n"
"Lighthouse still needs lighting...{page_break}"
"Agatio didn't think you'd be\n"
"coming back here, so I'm a\n"
"little surprised to see you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx02"
msgid "11486"
msgstr ""
"Agatio and Karst left for\n"
"Mars Lighthouse a little\n"
"while ago..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx03"
msgid "11487"
msgstr ""
"I'm glad you made it back\n"
"safely... The ice is making it very\n"
"difficult for anyone to sail here."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx04"
msgid "11488"
msgstr ""
"We're used to the cold up\n"
"here in Prox, but lately, it\n"
"seems to be getting worse."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx05"
msgid "11489"
msgstr ""
"I've been keeping a close\n"
"eye on the northern skies...{page_break}"
"Once I see a bright flash in\n"
"the distance, I'll know the\n"
"last beacon has been lit."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx06"
msgid "11490"
msgstr ""
"Have you seen Saturos or\n"
"Menardi? People have been\n"
"saying that they were killed..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx07"
msgid "11491"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, you're back? And you\n"
"learned how to use Psynergy?{page_break}"
"I can sense the power\n"
"inside of you... It's strong!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx08"
msgid "11492"
msgstr ""
"Once the final lighthouse is lit,\n"
"the winds should weaken. They\n"
"keep getting stronger, though!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx09"
msgid "11493"
msgstr ""
"Agatio and Karst told me that\n"
"{actor_name:5} ran away because\n"
"their quest was too dangerous."

msgctxt "MsgProx10"
msgid "11494"
msgstr ""
"Agatio and Karst are the\n"
"strongest fighters in Prox...\n"
"That's why we sent them.{page_break}"
"But I'm worried... They've been\n"
"gone for a while now, and the\n"
"lighthouse still remains dark.{end_wait} "

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx11"
msgid "11495"
msgstr ""
"Ever since Agatio returned from\n"
"Jupiter Lighthouse, the winds\n"
"have been stronger than ever..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx12"
msgid "11496"
msgstr ""
"It gets cold around here, but\n"
"this is the first time I've ever\n"
"seen snow pile up on the river.{page_break}"
"What if Agatio doesn't reach\n"
"Mars Lighthouse in time?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx13"
msgid "11497"
msgstr ""
"Everything is supposed to\n"
"return to normal once Mars\n"
"Lighthouse is lit again."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx14"
msgid "11498"
msgstr ""
"I can't believe anyone could\n"
"have beaten Saturos and\n"
"Menardi..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx15"
msgid "11499"
msgstr ""
"If {actor_name:5} could become an\n"
"Adept so quickly, so can I!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx16"
msgid "11500"
msgstr ""
"If this weather continues much\n"
"longer, we'll all be buried under\n"
"snow in no time."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx17"
msgid "11501"
msgstr ""
"The rift at Mars Lighthouse\n"
"gets wider every day.{page_break}"
"If we don't find a way to\n"
"stop it, I think it's going to\n"
"devour Prox entirely!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx18"
msgid "11502"
msgstr ""
"Our chieftain told me that the\n"
"rift is growing larger by the day,\n"
"just like Gaia Falls is.{page_break}"
"We'd better light the Mars\n"
"beacon soon, or Prox is\n"
"finished..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx19"
msgid "11503"
msgstr ""
"Not too long ago, I climbed\n"
"the mountains to the north to\n"
"look at the rift. It was huge!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx20"
msgid "11504"
msgstr ""
"I thought Prox would be here\n"
"forever, but now, it looks like\n"
"it might be destroyed!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx21"
msgid "11505"
msgstr ""
"Nobody believed that the rift\n"
"would go as far south as\n"
"Prox...{page_break}"
"They all thought Puelle was\n"
"being melodramatic... But no\n"
"one thinks that anymore..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx22"
msgid "11506"
msgstr ""
"The northern rift has gotten\n"
"so big that I couldn't see the\n"
"other side..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx23"
msgid "11507"
msgstr ""
"Prox originally flourished\n"
"because concerned Adepts lit\n"
"the fires of the Mars Lighthouse.{page_break}"
"Now, we, the people of the\n"
"northern flame, have been\n"
"forgotten by the outside world."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx24"
msgid "11508"
msgstr ""
"No one thought about our\n"
"needs when they extinguished\n"
"the great lighthouses...{page_break}"
"Now, because of them, our\n"
"great land is dying, crumbling\n"
"away at the edges..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx25"
msgid "11509"
msgstr ""
"If Mars Lighthouse's fires are\n"
"not rekindled, Prox will be\n"
"destroyed, but that's not all...{page_break}"
"Eventually, Gaia Falls will\n"
"continue to erode, finally\n"
"devouring all of Weyard."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx26"
msgid "11510"
msgstr ""
"When the lighthouses were\n"
"all extinguished, every great\n"
"civilization faded away..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx27"
msgid "11511"
msgstr ""
"To think that we all once\n"
"had the power to control\n"
"nature... What fools we were."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx28"
msgid "11512"
msgstr ""
"I think it's too late for us\n"
"already... But if they light the\n"
"fires, we'll be ready for them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx29"
msgid "11513"
msgstr ""
"We sent emissaries to Vale\n"
"to tell them that Weyard\n"
"was dying.{page_break}"
"But they wouldn't listen to us...\n"
"If only they had listened to us..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx30"
msgid "11514"
msgstr ""
"Vale's elders were stubborn...\n"
"They refused to listen to us,\n"
"and they drove us out by force.{page_break}"
"We had gone in peace, hoping\n"
"to convince them of the plight\n"
"our world faces..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx31"
msgid "11515"
msgstr ""
"At least the journey wasn't\n"
"for nothing. We learned that Sol\n"
"Sanctum held a hidden secret."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx32"
msgid "11516"
msgstr ""
"Three years ago, we sent our\n"
"finest to Sol Sanctum. All but\n"
"two were killed in a trap.{page_break}"
"The people of Vale couldn't\n"
"possibly understand how dire\n"
"our need was..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx33"
msgid "11517"
msgstr "{actor_name:5}, you like igloos, right?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11518"
msgstr ""
"You {text_effect:2}would{reset_text_style} say that...\n"
"You come from somewhere\n"
"warm and sunny!{page_break}"
"We didn't have anything to\n"
"play with, so we just decided\n"
"to make this thing..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11519"
msgstr ""
"Well, if you don't like cold\n"
"things, you're in the wrong\n"
"place!{page_break}"
"We just built this so that\n"
"we'd have something to\n"
"do to keep us warm..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx34"
msgid "11520"
msgstr ""
"The wind is so cold and\n"
"bitter that we decided to\n"
"hide out inside our igloo..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx35"
msgid "11521"
msgstr ""
"My parents told me that it\n"
"would do me good to get some\n"
"fresh air, but I'm freezing!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx36"
msgid "11522"
msgstr ""
"Those poor children. They\n"
"don't understand what's about\n"
"to happen to us...{page_break}"
"I just want them to be happy\n"
"in the short time left to us."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx37"
msgid "11523"
msgstr ""
"I hate igloos, but at least\n"
"it's protecting us from the\n"
"wind..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx38"
msgid "11524"
msgstr ""
"Mama and Papa have been\n"
"acting really strange lately...\n"
"They seem so sad.{page_break}"
"Whenever I ask them what's\n"
"wrong, they tell me to go\n"
"outside and play some more."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx39"
msgid "11525"
msgstr ""
"I always catch a cold when I'm\n"
"outside in weather like this...\n"
"Does Mom want me to get sick?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx40"
msgid "11526"
msgstr ""
"I can't bring myself to tell\n"
"them what's going to happen\n"
"to us...{pause_20_skippable} Oh, please, save us..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx41"
msgid "11527"
msgstr ""
"Puelle, our chieftain, grew\n"
"worried about Agatio and\n"
"Karst.{page_break}"
"He's gone to the northern\n"
"edge of town to wait for them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx42"
msgid "11528"
msgstr ""
"The people Saturos rescued\n"
"from the storm in Vale should\n"
"be waiting in their room.{page_break}"
"Once Mars Lighthouse has\n"
"been lit, they'll be free to\n"
"return home."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx43"
msgid "11529"
msgstr ""
"Don't forget, {actor_name:5}, your\n"
"mother and father are staying\n"
"in the north end of Prox."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx44"
msgid "11530"
msgstr ""
"Now that Saturos and his\n"
"team are gone, Agatio is the\n"
"last of our warriors.{page_break}"
"If something happens to\n"
"them, our final hope is lost."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx45"
msgid "11531"
msgstr ""
"Mars is the last lighthouse\n"
"that needs to be rekindled.{page_break}"
"Once that's been taken care\n"
"of, the people of Vale will be\n"
"set free."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx46"
msgid "11532"
msgstr ""
"Saturos used {actor_name:5}'s parents\n"
"to force {actor_name:5} to follow him\n"
"on his mission.{page_break}"
"We've fallen on hard times\n"
"when we need to coerce\n"
"people to join our cause."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx47"
msgid "11533"
msgstr "They're not here..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11534"
msgstr ""
"Strange... We looked all over\n"
"the village, and we can't find\n"
"any trace of them at all..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11535"
msgstr ""
"Everyone says they've\n"
"practically vanished without\n"
"a trace... It's so strange."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11536"
msgstr "You don't think they..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11537"
msgstr ""
"They wouldn't have gone to\n"
"the lighthouse..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11538"
msgstr "Yeah, you're probably right."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11539"
msgstr ""
"Puelle's going to be upset\n"
"that we didn't follow his\n"
"order to free them, though."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11540"
msgstr ""
"He was clear about it, too...\n"
"\"When {actor_name:5} returns to Prox,\n"
"set his parents free.\""

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx48"
msgid "11541"
msgstr ""
"Puelle ordered me to set\n"
"your parents free. That's\n"
"why I'm here now...{page_break}"
"The only thing is, no one\n"
"else is here... I don't know\n"
"where your parents went!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx49"
msgid "11542"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5} took the trouble of\n"
"coming back for his parents,\n"
"and now they're just gone?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx50"
msgid "11543"
msgstr ""
"Puelle wanted to set {actor_name:5}'s\n"
"parents free before Prox\n"
"was destroyed...{page_break}"
"But if we can't find them,\n"
"how can we set them free?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx51"
msgid "11544"
msgstr ""
"I can't think of anywhere\n"
"else {actor_name:5}'s parents\n"
"might have gone!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx52"
msgid "11545"
msgstr ""
"When you left Prox, you were\n"
"so young that you could barely\n"
"lift a sword!{page_break}"
"Now, look at you! You could\n"
"handle any weapon with ease!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx53"
msgid "11546"
msgstr ""
"You go away for a little\n"
"while, and you come back\n"
"a strong and mighty warrior!{page_break}"
"I'm so proud of you!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx54"
msgid "11547"
msgstr ""
"What has he gone through\n"
"that he's become so strong\n"
"in such a short time?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx55"
msgid "11548"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5} looks so confident,\n"
"so bold... You can see it in\n"
"his eyes..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx56"
msgid "11549"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, your parents have\n"
"gone away... They were very\n"
"worried about you."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx57"
msgid "11550"
msgstr ""
"Your mother knows that you're\n"
"strong and healthy, so I'm sure\n"
"she's very relieved..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx58"
msgid "11551"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}'s parents\n"
"were worried about him when\n"
"they heard Saturos was dead."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx59"
msgid "11552"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}'s parents were\n"
"so worried about him that\n"
"they were wasting away..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx60"
msgid "11553"
msgstr ""
"I hear Agatio and Karst have\n"
"gone to Mars Lighthouse...{page_break}"
"What if their actions only\n"
"cause more turmoil? How can\n"
"we be sure they're right?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx61"
msgid "11554"
msgstr ""
"These catastrophes are\n"
"the result of the lighthouse\n"
"beacons being rekindled.{page_break}"
"This snow, this wind, it all\n"
"started after Jupiter\n"
"Lighthouse was lit."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx62"
msgid "11555"
msgstr ""
"We can't wait for Agatio\n"
"and his men any longer..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11556"
msgstr ""
"If we wait much longer, this wind\n"
"and snow will make it impossible\n"
"to reach the lighthouse."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11557"
msgstr ""
"I'm going to the lighthouse...\n"
"Will any of you come\n"
"with me?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11558"
msgstr ""
"Puelle, I can't let you\n"
"go on your own..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11559"
msgstr ""
"If something were to\n"
"happen to you, who\n"
"would lead our village?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11560"
msgstr ""
"Please, you must let us\n"
"go in your stead."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11561"
msgstr ""
"How can you expect to\n"
"accomplish what Agatio\n"
"and Karst could not?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11562"
msgstr ""
"They may have been more\n"
"powerful than any of us, but\n"
"we can't just stand by!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11563"
msgstr ""
"They're not coming back,\n"
"just like Saturos... You have\n"
"to let us try."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11564"
msgstr "I can't. I can't allow it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11565"
msgstr ""
"Listen to your elder...\n"
"He speaks wisely."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11566"
msgstr "I'm speaking to you too, Puelle."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11567"
msgstr ""
"If Agatio and Karst cannot\n"
"do the task, how can you, a\n"
"single man, hope to do it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11568"
msgstr ""
"What are you saying?\n"
"If we stand around debating,\n"
"our town is doomed for certain!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11569"
msgstr ""
"We can't risk sacrificing\n"
"any more lives."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11570"
msgstr ""
"So, we must sit here and\n"
"wait for a miracle to come."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx63"
msgid "11571"
msgstr ""
"Is that you, {actor_name:5}? When\n"
"did you return to Prox?{page_break}"
"You should take your parents\n"
"back to Vale, so they can at\n"
"least die in their hometown."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx64"
msgid "11572"
msgstr ""
"If we were better Adepts,\n"
"we could try to enter the\n"
"lighthouse ourselves..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx65"
msgid "11573"
msgstr ""
"I feel so helpless... Agatio has\n"
"not returned, and the lighthouse\n"
"beacon remains unlit."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx66"
msgid "11574"
msgstr ""
"All we can do now is wait\n"
"for Agatio and his men to\n"
"return...{page_break}"
"But no honest soldier can\n"
"sit idly by while others do\n"
"all of the work."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx67"
msgid "11575"
msgstr ""
"Our Psynergy feels weak...\n"
"I can sense it inside me.{page_break}"
"The water, earth, and wind\n"
"lighthouses have been lit,\n"
"and fire alone remains dark."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx68"
msgid "11576"
msgstr ""
"Puelle promised that he\n"
"would return our hostages\n"
"to Vale.{page_break}"
"If you don't believe me,\n"
"ask him yourself."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx69"
msgid "11577"
msgstr ""
"If the lighthouse isn't lit\n"
"soon, Prox is doomed...\n"
"I need to get out of here!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx70"
msgid "11578"
msgstr ""
"Neither our elder nor Puelle\n"
"will tell us what's going on\n"
"at the lighthouse...{page_break}"
"Why are we training so\n"
"much? A lighthouse shouldn't\n"
"pose that much danger..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx71"
msgid "11579"
msgstr ""
"Puelle is stronger than any\n"
"of us, and there is nothing\n"
"he can do to save us...{page_break}"
"But if we don't take some\n"
"kind of action, Prox will be\n"
"destroyed for sure..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx72"
msgid "11580"
msgstr ""
"If they didn't light the beacon\n"
"and they didn't return home,\n"
"Agatio's team must have failed."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx73"
msgid "11581"
msgstr ""
"If only my fire Psynergy\n"
"weren't so weak now, I\n"
"might be able to help..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx74"
msgid "11582"
msgstr ""
"Puelle never intended to take\n"
"hostages. He wanted the people\n"
"of Vale to be returned safely.{page_break}"
"Saturos insisted that we\n"
"hold on to them for our\n"
"safety, but Puelle disagreed."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx75"
msgid "11583"
msgstr "You... {actor_name:5}, it's you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11584"
msgstr ""
"I'd heard that you had returned\n"
"to us... You look so much\n"
"stronger than when you left."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11585"
msgstr ""
"It seems he has brought\n"
"some allies with him."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11586"
msgstr "Yes... I am Kraden."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11587"
msgstr "My name is {actor_name:1}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11588"
msgstr "{actor_name:1}... Isn't that..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11589"
msgstr ""
"That is the name of the one\n"
"Agatio said had killed Saturos\n"
"and Menardi."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11590"
msgstr "{actor_name:1}, stop that..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11591"
msgstr ""
"You are correct, but\n"
"{actor_name:1} had reasons\n"
"for fighting them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11592"
msgstr ""
"Saturos and Menardi had\n"
"invaded Vale, stolen its sacred\n"
"treasure, triggered a volcano..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11593"
msgstr ""
"You cannot blame {actor_name:1} for\n"
"pursuing them and fighting\n"
"to regain what they had stolen."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11594"
msgstr ""
"We only wanted to stop them...\n"
"We didn't think they'd fight\n"
"us to the death."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11595"
msgstr ""
"They flung themselves into the\n"
"opening of Venus Lighthouse's\n"
"beacon..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11596"
msgstr ""
"Did...Saturos and Menardi\n"
"put up a good fight?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11597"
msgstr ""
"I'll bet you thought you\n"
"didn't stand a chance\n"
"against them, huh?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11598"
msgstr ""
"You were probably really\n"
"tense the whole time..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11599"
msgstr ""
"Saturos and Menardi had a\n"
"job to do... That was all."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11600"
msgstr ""
"If I'd been in your shoes, I'd\n"
"have done the same thing...\n"
"I can't blame you."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11601"
msgstr ""
"And in the end, you were stronger\n"
"than they were... You should be\n"
"proud of that."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11602"
msgstr ""
"I am sad that they lost their\n"
"lives in their quest, but there\n"
"was no avoiding it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11603"
msgstr ""
"What has happened cannot\n"
"be undone. We should cooperate\n"
"to find a way to save Weyard."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11604"
msgstr ""
"We understand that Agatio\n"
"and Karst have made for Mars\n"
"Lighthouse and not returned."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11605"
msgstr ""
"Then all that remains for us\n"
"is to wait until Gaia Falls\n"
"carries us all to our doom."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11606"
msgstr ""
"It seems that Mars Lighthouse\n"
"is as dangerous as all the rest."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11607"
msgstr ""
"We have only a few soldiers\n"
"remaining, and none who can\n"
"make the climb to the aerie."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11608"
msgstr ""
"Only Saturos and perhaps\n"
"Agatio were strong enough\n"
"to reach the top..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11609"
msgstr ""
"And none of them can\n"
"help us now."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11610"
msgstr "You think we can do it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11611"
msgstr "I agree, {actor_name:5}..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11612"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, what are you\n"
"thinking?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11613"
msgstr ""
"We've climbed three lighthouses\n"
"already... What's one more? Let's\n"
"go to Mars Lighthouse!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11614"
msgstr ""
"They've proven themselves\n"
"strong enough! I say we trust\n"
"in {actor_name:5} to do this!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11615"
msgstr ""
"This is an unexpected turn of\n"
"events, but yes, I think you\n"
"can light the lighthouse..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11616"
msgstr ""
"Off to the Mars Lighthouse!\n"
"Let's go, {actor_name:5}!\n"
"Come on, {actor_name:1}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11617"
msgstr ""
"There is one thing that I\n"
"don't want you to forget."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11618"
msgstr ""
"In order to light the beacon\n"
"at Mars Lighthouse, you will\n"
"need to have the Mars Star."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11619"
msgstr ""
"Ah! And Agatio and Karst\n"
"have the Mars Star now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11620"
msgstr ""
"You must find Agatio and\n"
"Karst, and you must take\n"
"the Mars Star from them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11621"
msgstr ""
"Thanks for your help.\n"
"The future of Weyard\n"
"rests in your hands."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx76"
msgid "11622"
msgstr ""
"You must find Karst,\n"
"get the Mars Star, and\n"
"light the lighthouse."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx77"
msgid "11623"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, you are the only\n"
"hope left to us now.\n"
"Good luck."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx78"
msgid "11624"
msgstr ""
"If this doesn't work, we're all\n"
"finished... Prox, Weyard, even\n"
"Vale... All will be lost..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx79"
msgid "11625"
msgstr ""
"If they were strong enough to\n"
"defeat Saturos and Menardi,\n"
"perhaps they can do the job..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMarsStar01"
msgid "11626"
msgstr "Why... Why am I lying here?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11627"
msgstr ""
"Wait, I think I remember... We\n"
"were going to light the beacon..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11628"
msgstr ""
"But the lighthouse was frozen.\n"
"We wandered lost inside,\n"
"trying to find the aerie..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11629"
msgstr ""
"We must hurry... If we\n"
"delay, Prox is destroyed."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11630"
msgstr ""
"It's no use... I'm absolutely\n"
"drained... I can't even stand."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11631"
msgstr ""
"And the cold... Why am I so cold?\n"
"We of the Fire Clan are meant\n"
"to be immune to the cold..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11632"
msgstr ""
"I feel the cold too, Karst...\n"
"I... I'm afraid we're going\n"
"to die up here..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11633"
msgstr ""
"I can feel it now... The long,\n"
"dark sleep creeping into\n"
"my soul..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11634"
msgstr ""
"Wait... I think\n"
"I remember..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11635"
msgstr ""
"The eye... It told us that we\n"
"lack the will to go any farther."

msgctxt "message"
msgid "11636"
msgstr ""
"The eye... I remember now...\n"
"I felt its gaze pierce me to\n"
"the core, then all went black...{end_wait} "

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11637"
msgstr ""
"That's right... And I remember\n"
"fighting against {actor_name:5}..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11638"
msgstr ""
"I do, too... Was it a dream?\n"
"An illusion?"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11639"
msgstr "{actor_name:5}? Is that you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11640"
msgstr ""
"Amazing... Then our luck hasn't\n"
"entirely run out yet..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11641"
msgstr ""
"How can you play games\n"
"with us like this?{page_break}"
"Regardless, it's amazing that\n"
"you're here... It means our luck\n"
"hasn't entirely run out yet..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11642"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, you must complete\n"
"our quest... Please... You have\n"
"to light the beacon..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11643"
msgstr ""
"We can't even stand... We're in\n"
"no condition to go on. Light\n"
"the beacon for us... Please."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11644"
msgstr ""
"You'll need the Mars Star.\n"
"Go on... Take it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11645"
msgstr ""
"Please hurry... If I can just see\n"
"the light of the beacon, I'll know\n"
"that I haven't died in vain."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11646"
msgstr "We're counting on you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMarsStar02"
msgid "11647"
msgstr ""
"It's too late for us now...\n"
"Hurry, light the beacon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMarsStar03"
msgid "11648"
msgstr ""
"Your hand...so warm...\n"
"People have such warm\n"
"hands... I had forgotten..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMarsStar04"
msgid "11649"
msgstr ""
"I'm so tired... A fog is rising\n"
"before my eyes... No! Can't\n"
"die until the beacon...is lit..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMarsStar05"
msgid "11650"
msgstr ""
"I'm so cold, colder than I ever\n"
"thought possible... All because\n"
"Mars Lighthouse remains unlit...{page_break}"
"I have to stay alive...long\n"
"enough to see its light..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMarsStar06"
msgid "11651"
msgstr ""
"You who hold the star,\n"
"open your heart and listen...{page_break}"
"If you wish to reach the heavens,\n"
"give your star to me."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIfYouDo"
msgid "11652"
msgstr ""
"If you do not hold the star,\n"
"you shall not ascend to the\n"
"heavens... Begone!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgYouWhoHold"
msgid "11653"
msgstr ""
"You who hold the star,\n"
"open your heart and listen..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11654"
msgstr ""
"If you wish to scale the\n"
"heavens, set the four\n"
"spirits aflame!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMankindWithThe"
msgid "11655"
msgstr ""
"Mankind... With the power of\n"
"wisdom, they ruled the earth."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgFishWithCold"
msgid "11656"
msgstr ""
"Fish... With cold courage,\n"
"they ruled the water."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgDragonsBurningWith"
msgid "11657"
msgstr ""
"Dragons... Burning with might,\n"
"they ruled the fires."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgBirdOnThe"
msgid "11658"
msgstr ""
"Bird... On the wings of truth,\n"
"they ruled the winds."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgYouHaveProven"
msgid "11659"
msgstr ""
"You have proven your worth!\n"
"The heavens await you!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgBetrayersYouHave"
msgid "11660"
msgstr "Betrayers, you have arrived!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11661"
msgstr "Who said that!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11662"
msgstr ""
"The wind's too strong!\n"
"I can't see anything!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11663"
msgstr ""
"I heard it too, but I don't\n"
"see anyone else up here!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11664"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}! Quick! Cast the Mars\n"
"Star in before anything\n"
"has a chance to stop us!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11665"
msgstr ""
"So, you are still intent on lighting\n"
"the beacon of Mars Lighthouse?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11666"
msgstr "Who said that!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11667"
msgstr ""
"Have you forgotten me so soon,\n"
"{actor_name:1}? And you, {actor_name:2}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11668"
msgstr ""
"It seems to know you,\n"
"{actor_name:1}... Do you have any\n"
"idea what it is?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11669"
msgstr "Then search your heart, boy!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11670"
msgstr "That voice..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11671"
msgstr "It's...the Wise One!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11672"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}, since when are\n"
"you on a first-name basis\n"
"with the Wise One?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11673"
msgstr ""
"It must have "
"been{pause_20_skippable}.{pause_20_skippable}.{pause_20_skippable}. "
"{actor_name:1},\n"
"what happened in Sol Sanctum\n"
"after we were kidnapped?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11674"
msgstr ""
"When Saturos and Menardi stole\n"
"the Elemental Stars, they also\n"
"triggered a volcanic eruption.{page_break}"
"The Wise One prevented Mt. Aleph\n"
"from erupting so that {actor_name:2}\n"
"and I could escape."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11675"
msgstr ""
"But...wait, Mt. Aleph {text_effect:2}did{reset_text_style} erupt!\n"
"There was a huge explosion! We\n"
"saw it all the way in Vault!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11676"
msgstr ""
"But it would have erupted with\n"
"us still inside... There was no way\n"
"we could have escaped in time."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11677"
msgstr ""
"The Wise One held off the\n"
"eruption until we could escape...\n"
"He even halted the lava flow."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11678"
msgstr ""
"I can't believe it... Nobody has\n"
"enough power to do that..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11679"
msgstr ""
"I know it sounds weird, but I\n"
"was there, and it happened, so\n"
"you'll just have to believe us!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11680"
msgstr ""
"If it can do all that, this\n"
"Wise One seems more like\n"
"a god than an Adept!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11681"
msgstr ""
"I did not just save you. I also\n"
"tasked you with recovering the\n"
"four Elemental Stars."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11682"
msgstr ""
"Why have you disobeyed my\n"
"command? Why have you come\n"
"to light the beacon?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11683"
msgstr ""
"Because Prox will be\n"
"destroyed if we don't! We\n"
"can't let that happen..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11684"
msgstr ""
"Prox? They have brought this\n"
"disaster upon themselves."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11685"
msgstr ""
"Are you saying we should just\n"
"abandon them to die? What\n"
"did they do to deserve that!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11686"
msgstr ""
"The people of Prox have\n"
"committed an unforgivable\n"
"sin. They must pay the price."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11687"
msgstr ""
"For lighting the lighthouses?\n"
"Is that their sin? Does that\n"
"warrant total destruction?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11688"
msgstr ""
"If we don't light the beacon,\n"
"Gaia Falls will eventually\n"
"erode away all of Weyard!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11689"
msgstr ""
"We have fought for so long to\n"
"save all the people of our world,\n"
"and now you would stop us?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11690"
msgstr ""
"Gaia Falls is growing.\n"
"It's consuming more and\n"
"more with each passing day!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11691"
msgstr ""
"How can you just allow\n"
"the world to crumble into\n"
"nothingness?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11692"
msgstr ""
"The seal needs to be\n"
"broken! The world will be\n"
"destroyed if it's not!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11693"
msgstr ""
"You have learned\n"
"far too much."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11694"
msgstr ""
"Wise One! You can't continue\n"
"to protect the lighthouses! You\n"
"know what's happening!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11695"
msgstr ""
"It is your duty to protect all of\n"
"Weyard! If Weyard is destroyed,\n"
"you will have failed us all!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11696"
msgstr ""
"Why won't you answer\n"
"us, Wise One?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11697"
msgstr ""
"If Alchemy is unleashed,\n"
"mankind may well destroy\n"
"all of Weyard itself."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11698"
msgstr ""
"But we can combine our\n"
"strengths, ensure that Alchemy\n"
"not be used for evil..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11699"
msgstr ""
"It is inevitable. In time, one man\n"
"will seek to rule over all. It is\n"
"human nature, inescapable."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11700"
msgstr ""
"And it shall come sooner\n"
"than any of you think."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11701"
msgstr "Why do you say that?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11702"
msgstr ""
"The Water Adept who climbs\n"
"toward the peak of Mt. Aleph\n"
"even as we speak...{page_break}"
"Is he not a friend of yours?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11703"
msgstr ""
"Alex is his name. Surely,\n"
"you have not forgotten him?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11704"
msgstr ""
"Alex!? What would he be\n"
"doing on Mt. Aleph?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11705"
msgstr ""
"He understands far more than\n"
"you do. He knows that when\n"
"the four beacons have been lit...{page_break}"
"Their light will gather\n"
"at Sol Sanctum."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11706"
msgstr ""
"But what would he gain\n"
"from being there?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11707"
msgstr ""
"When the final beam of light\n"
"reaches the peak of Mt. Aleph,\n"
"the Golden Sun shall rise."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11708"
msgstr ""
"The Golden Sun!?\n"
"What is that? And what\n"
"would Alex want with it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11709"
msgstr ""
"When the four beams merge\n"
"into one, they form a golden\n"
"light, bathing Mt. Aleph's peak."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11710"
msgstr ""
"Is... Is that Alchemy? I mean,\n"
"pure Alchemy made real, at\n"
"the heart of its power?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11711"
msgstr ""
"And it's that light that gives\n"
"shape to the Stone of Sages?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11712"
msgstr ""
"This has been Alex's one true\n"
"desire from the very start."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11713"
msgstr ""
"Alex planned all of this?\n"
"Then he must have been\n"
"after this power all along!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11714"
msgstr ""
"We've been duped! He used us all!\n"
"Oh, you'd better believe he's\n"
"not getting away with this!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11715"
msgstr ""
"Alex... How could he do this?\n"
"He's... He's one of my own\n"
"people! I feel sick...disgusted..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11716"
msgstr ""
"None of that matters right now.\n"
"We still have to light the beacon.\n"
"We don't have any choice."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11717"
msgstr ""
"If we don't do it now, Prox\n"
"will be destroyed!\n"
"{actor_name:5}... We have to, right?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11718"
msgstr ""
"You bet we do! The Wise One\n"
"will have to deal with Alex\n"
"on his own."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11719"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}! We don't have any\n"
"choice! The Wise One will have\n"
"to deal with Alex himself."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11720"
msgstr ""
"I cannot interfere in the\n"
"actions of mankind."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11721"
msgstr ""
"If you can't interfere, then how\n"
"about getting out of our way so\n"
"we can light the beacon, huh?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11722"
msgstr "Ooo... Good one, {actor_name:6}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11723"
msgstr ""
"I don't like doing exactly what\n"
"Alex wants, but it's looking like\n"
"we've got no choice..."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11724"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry, {actor_name:5}!\n"
"Just throw the Mars Star into\n"
"the beacon's well! Now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11725"
msgstr ""
"The Wise One himself said\n"
"he's not allowed to interfere!\n"
"You're all clear!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11726"
msgstr ""
"Wise One! Didn't you just say\n"
"that you aren't allowed to\n"
"interfere with our actions?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11727"
msgstr ""
"That is correct.\n"
"I cannot stop you."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11728"
msgstr ""
"But...what if some miracle were\n"
"to occur, one that prevented you\n"
"from igniting the beacon?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11729"
msgstr ""
"Miracle? What are you talking\n"
"about? What kind of miracle?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11730"
msgstr ""
"If you can defeat a miracle,\n"
"only then can you ignite the\n"
"beacon's flame."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11731"
msgstr ""
"The Wise One is up to something!\n"
"Be wary, everyone! We don't\n"
"know what he's capable of!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11732"
msgstr ""
"A three-headed dragon?\n"
"{text_effect:2}That's{reset_text_style} your miracle?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11733"
msgstr ""
"So you would have us fight\n"
"for our future? Fine, then\n"
"fight we shall!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11734"
msgstr ""
"What's he thinking? We already\n"
"beat a two-headed dragon. How\n"
"much tougher can this one be?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11735"
msgstr ""
"I don't care how many heads\n"
"it has. Nothing's going to\n"
"stop us now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11736"
msgstr ""
"Let's do it! For Prox!\n"
"For the future of Weyard!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11737"
msgstr ""
"Wait a second... Wasn't that\n"
"two-headed dragon "
"actually{pause_20_skippable}.{pause_20_skippable}.{pause_20_skippable}."
"{page_break}"
"So that means this three-\n"
"headed dragon must be..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11738"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}! NO! You mustn't\n"
"fight that dragon! It's°"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11739"
msgstr ""
"Too late, Kraden! We can't\n"
"get away from it now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11740"
msgstr "{actor_name:5}, don't! Stop!!!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWhoAreThey"
msgid "11741"
msgstr "...Who are they?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11742"
msgstr ""
"That's what I was trying\n"
"to warn you about!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11743"
msgstr ""
"It wasn't just the dragon\n"
"you killed..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11744"
msgstr ""
"I remember you warning us,\n"
"but it was too late for us to\n"
"stop..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11745"
msgstr ""
"Kraden, what do you know?\n"
"Why were you trying to stop\n"
"us from fighting the dragon?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11746"
msgstr ""
"It was the Wise One's\n"
"final trap..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11747"
msgstr "Trap? What do you mean?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11748"
msgstr ""
"The Wise One knew he couldn't\n"
"stop you, so he played a cruel,\n"
"wretched trick on you instead."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11749"
msgstr ""
"Kraden, I don't understand...\n"
"What are you trying to tell us?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11750"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:7}, let's see who\n"
"those people are while they\n"
"try to sort this out."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11751"
msgstr ""
"No, {actor_name:6}! Don't look!\n"
"You mustn't look! It will only\n"
"bring you pain..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11752"
msgstr ""
"What are you talking about,\n"
"Kraden? They can't hurt us\n"
"anymore... We'll just°"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11753"
msgstr "What's the matter, {actor_name:6}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11754"
msgstr "It...can't be... How? How..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11755"
msgstr "Nnn... Uhnnn..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11756"
msgstr "What is it, {actor_name:1}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11757"
msgstr "Uhhh...unnnn..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11758"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}! I... I know\n"
"that guy! That's your dad!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11759"
msgstr ""
"Then...does that mean...\n"
"the other two are..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11760"
msgstr "Hhnnnng..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11761"
msgstr "Hhhnnn..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11762"
msgstr "Mom... Dad..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11763"
msgstr ""
"I'll heal {actor_name:6}'s parents!\n"
"Quickly, {actor_name:4}! Tend to\n"
"{actor_name:1}'s father!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11764"
msgstr ""
"If only... If only I'd realized\n"
"it sooner..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWhatSTheMatter"
msgid "11765"
msgstr ""
"What's the matter, {actor_name:8}?\n"
"Why did you stop? {actor_name:6}'s\n"
"parents need you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11766"
msgstr ""
"Don't give up, {actor_name:4}. You\n"
"can't! You have to save them..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11767"
msgstr ""
"It's no use, {actor_name:3}...\n"
"I'm tapped..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11768"
msgstr ""
"I am, too... And even if I weren't,{pause_20_skippable}\n"
"it's just too late..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11769"
msgstr "What are you saying!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11770"
msgstr ""
"They're not...\n"
"They can't be..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11771"
msgstr ""
"That's not what I'm saying,\n"
"{actor_name:6}... I..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11772"
msgstr ""
"I finally found them... I was\n"
"going to be with them again...\n"
"For the first time in years..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11773"
msgstr "{actor_name:6}..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11774"
msgstr "Please... It can't be..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11775"
msgstr ""
"Mom... Wake up!\n"
"It's me... It's {actor_name:6}!\n"
"...Don't leave me..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11776"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:6}, you must prepare\n"
"yourself for what comes next..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11777"
msgstr ""
"Being transformed into a dragon,\n"
"fighting in that form... This\n"
"requires tremendous power."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11778"
msgstr "What are you saying, Kraden?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11779"
msgstr ""
"In fighting you, your parents\n"
"were forced to use every\n"
"last ounce of their energy."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11780"
msgstr "They don't have the strength to..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11781"
msgstr ""
"Even if they had won the battle,\n"
"they would not have survived.\n"
"You cannot blame yourself..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11782"
msgstr "You monster!!!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11783"
msgstr ""
"Why did you do this? Why\n"
"did you make us fight\n"
"{actor_name:6}'s parents?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11784"
msgstr ""
"You're no god! You're no\n"
"protector! You're evil!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11785"
msgstr ""
"You don't understand the pain\n"
"you have caused, Wise One."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11786"
msgstr ""
"You have no idea the damage\n"
"done to a child who learns she\n"
"has destroyed her own parents."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11787"
msgstr "That's enough..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11788"
msgstr ""
"I knew what I was doing the\n"
"moment I raised my sword."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11789"
msgstr ""
"We defied the Wise One in\n"
"order to save the world.\n"
"Our parents would understand."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11790"
msgstr "Don't you think so, {actor_name:5}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11791"
msgstr ""
"You're right. It hurts, but it's true.\n"
"We didn't do this for ourselves.\n"
"We did it for all of Weyard."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11792"
msgstr ""
"I agree with my brother...\n"
"But it does no one any good\n"
"if we don't complete our task."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11793"
msgstr ""
"We still have a chance to\n"
"save Prox."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11794"
msgstr ""
"Perhaps we can't save your\n"
"parents, but we can save\n"
"countless others."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11795"
msgstr ""
"Kyle and the others saved\n"
"them, too... They sacrificed their\n"
"lives so that we could go on."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11796"
msgstr ""
"I never imagined that\n"
"my actions would help\n"
"to save the world..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11797"
msgstr ""
"Even though lighting the beacon\n"
"may create wars and strife,\n"
"I regret none of this."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11798"
msgstr ""
"There's little time left, {actor_name:5}...\n"
"Use the Mars Star and\n"
"light the beacon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgOurQuestIs"
msgid "11799"
msgstr ""
"Our quest is almost over.\n"
"I...don't know how I'm going\n"
"to tell Mom about this...{page_break}"
"But sorrow can wait. We've\n"
"got to light the beacon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIWishICould"
msgid "11800"
msgstr ""
"I wish I could console you\n"
"somehow... It must be tough...{page_break}"
"I just wish I'd had one last\n"
"chance to have some of\n"
"{actor_name:5}'s mother's cookies."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIUnderstandYour"
msgid "11801"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, I understand your\n"
"loss...{page_break}"
"But remember, you and {actor_name:6}\n"
"still have each other."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIfAlexSet"
msgid "11802"
msgstr ""
"If Alex set this all in motion,\n"
"then he's responsible for this,\n"
"and I'll never forgive him."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIThoughtID"
msgid "11803"
msgstr ""
"I thought I'd get to see my\n"
"parents again... I thought I'd\n"
"get to hold them again...{page_break}"
"But instead, we were\n"
"forced to destroy them..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIDonTKnowMy"
msgid "11804"
msgstr ""
"I don't know my parents...\n"
"They might be alive, somewhere\n"
"out there... But I share your pain."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIMSorryThings"
msgid "11805"
msgstr ""
"I'm sorry things had to end\n"
"up like this, {actor_name:6}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgBothKyleAnd"
msgid "11806"
msgstr ""
"Both Kyle and your parents\n"
"were very dear to me. My\n"
"sorrow joins yours, friends.{page_break}"
"We must light the beacon, if for\n"
"no other reason than to provide\n"
"them with a proper funeral."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgUnnnnIAm"
msgid "11807"
msgstr ""
"Unnnn... {actor_name:5}?\n"
"...{actor_name:6}?{page_break}"
"I am so happy...to have one\n"
"last chance to see you again...\n"
"in the end..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgUhhhhnnnICan"
msgid "11808"
msgstr ""
"Uhhhhnnn... {actor_name:5}...\n"
"I...can't see you, but I sense that\n"
"you're nearby...{page_break}"
"Please... Take care of\n"
"{actor_name:6} for us..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgKoffKoffYou"
msgid "11809"
msgstr ""
"*Koff! Koff!* {actor_name:5}...\n"
"You made it back...alive...\n"
"Please, I must ask one last thing...{page_break}"
"Tell Dora...to live her life\n"
"to the fullest...for me..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgDoNotLet"
msgid "11810"
msgstr ""
"Do not let your sadness\n"
"overwhelm you, {actor_name:5}!{page_break}"
"Go! Once the beacon has been\n"
"ignited, you can mourn as much\n"
"as you need. I will protect you."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "MsgWillYouCast"
msgid "11811"
msgstr "Will you cast in the Mars Star?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgTheBeaconIs"
msgid "11812"
msgstr "The beacon is lit!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11813"
msgstr ""
"And to think, I joined this quest\n"
"hoping to prevent exactly this\n"
"from happening..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11814"
msgstr ""
"And I began this quest as a\n"
"prisoner, taken against my will."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11815"
msgstr ""
"And if that tidal wave hadn't\n"
"sent me far off course, I\n"
"wouldn't even be here now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11816"
msgstr ""
"How many lives have been\n"
"taken and changed forever\n"
"just to light this beacon?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11817"
msgstr ""
"Mom... Dad...\n"
"Weyard is safe now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11818"
msgstr ""
"You're right!\n"
"I hear voices, too!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11819"
msgstr ""
"I told you...\n"
"I told you I could hear them!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11820"
msgstr ""
"Who said that?\n"
"Where are you?!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11821"
msgstr ""
"We're in Imil! We're at the\n"
"base of Mercury Lighthouse!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11822"
msgstr "You... You can't be!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgImilVoicesDisbeliefReply"
msgid "11823"
msgstr "You... You can't be!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11824"
msgstr ""
"Hey! I know that voice!\n"
"It's {actor_name:4}, I just\n"
"know it!{pause_20_skippable} {actor_name:4}!!!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11825"
msgstr "It's you!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11826"
msgstr ""
"Of course it's us! We can hear\n"
"you, {actor_name:4}! You're all\n"
"right! I'm so happy!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11827"
msgstr ""
"Who are those two\n"
"kids talking to?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11828"
msgstr ""
"I don't know. They've been\n"
"standing here telling everyone\n"
"to leave the lighthouse.{page_break}"
"...Weird couple of kids\n"
"if you ask me!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11829"
msgstr ""
"How is it that we\n"
"can hear you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11830"
msgstr ""
"I don't know, but he told us\n"
"we'd be able to talk to you\n"
"if we came here now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11831"
msgstr "He? Who's \"he\"?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11832"
msgstr ""
"I don't know... We were sleeping,\n"
"and he came to us in a dream...{page_break}"
"He said, \"Go to the lighthouse!\""

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11833"
msgstr "The lighthouse? Why?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11834"
msgstr ""
"He said that we have to\n"
"deliver a message... He was\n"
"too busy to do it himself..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11835"
msgstr "What message?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11836"
msgstr ""
"We have to warn everyone to\n"
"stay clear of the lighthouses!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11837"
msgstr "What's going to happen?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11838"
msgstr ""
"I don't know, but he told us\n"
"to warn people away from\n"
"Mt. Aleph as well!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11839"
msgstr ""
"But who is \"he\"!? You\n"
"still haven't told us!!!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11840"
msgstr ""
"You're a meanie! I don't\n"
"tell meanies anything!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11841"
msgstr ""
"Don't pay any attention to\n"
"him... It's me, {actor_name:4}... Can you\n"
"tell me who spoke to you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11842"
msgstr ""
"I told you, I don't know, but\n"
"he looked like a big rock...\n"
"with a big, rocky eye!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11843"
msgstr "The... The Wise One!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWhatCouldHe"
msgid "11844"
msgstr "What could he be doing?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11845"
msgstr "Of course! I understand..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11846"
msgstr ""
"The Wise One said that when\n"
"all four lighthouses have been\n"
"lit, the Golden Sun will shine..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11847"
msgstr ""
"When that happens, Mt. Aleph\n"
"and the lighthouses will probably\n"
"become quite dangerous..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11848"
msgstr ""
"So, the Wise One is warning\n"
"people in dreams, telling\n"
"them to seek refuge?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11849"
msgstr ""
"Why would he do that!? You\n"
"saw what he did to us... He\n"
"can't be up to anything good..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11850"
msgstr ""
"Have you not learned?\n"
"One's actions do not always\n"
"reveal one's true intentions."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11851"
msgstr "Hamma...{pause_20_skippable} Sister..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11852"
msgstr ""
"Master Hamma! Did you receive\n"
"a message, too?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11853"
msgstr ""
"Yes. I was called to Jupiter\n"
"Lighthouse in a dream."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11854"
msgstr ""
"You have completed your\n"
"quest, but I see it comes\n"
"with great loss...{page_break}"
"Your suffering has been\n"
"almost unbearable."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11855"
msgstr "Master Hamma... My parents..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11856"
msgstr ""
"I know, {actor_name:6}, and I am sorry.\n"
"But do not give up hope\n"
"for them just yet..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11857"
msgstr ""
"What do you mean,\n"
"Master Hamma?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11858"
msgstr ""
"Appearances can be an\n"
"illusion... The Wise One\n"
"has a caring heart."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11859"
msgstr ""
"He forced us to fight\n"
"{actor_name:1}'s and {actor_name:6}'s parents!\n"
"What's so \"caring\" about that!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11860"
msgstr ""
"If the Wise One were truly evil,\n"
"he would not be warning me\n"
"of danger in my dreams."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11861"
msgstr ""
"Well, I... I guess not... But\n"
"then, what's he up to?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11862"
msgstr ""
"We do not have time to\n"
"discuss it right now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11863"
msgstr ""
"She's right.{page_break}"
"If the Wise One said it's not\n"
"safe to be near the lighthouses,\n"
"then I think we should listen."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11864"
msgstr ""
"I am heading for safety, too.\n"
"All of you must get away\n"
"from the lighthouse now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11865"
msgstr "Hurry, everyone! Let's go!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11866"
msgstr "What about our parents?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11867"
msgstr "We can't leave them behind..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11868"
msgstr ""
"I understand how you feel, but\n"
"we won't make it if we have\n"
"to take them with us!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11869"
msgstr ""
"Make the decision, {actor_name:5}!\n"
"Should we take them with us?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11870"
msgstr ""
"It's too dangerous...\n"
"The Golden Sun is forming!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11871"
msgstr ""
"A ray of light is emanating\n"
"from the beacon... From the\n"
"Mars Star."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11872"
msgstr "What will happen?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11873"
msgstr ""
"The power of Alchemy will\n"
"be unleashed upon the world!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11874"
msgstr ""
"We must take {actor_name:1}'s\n"
"father and {actor_name:6}'s\n"
"parents and flee!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11875"
msgstr "Stop it! Let go of my wrist!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11876"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:2}, get a grip!\n"
"No one's touching you!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11877"
msgstr "I'm serious! I..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11878"
msgstr "The beacon!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11879"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:6}... We have to\n"
"move your parents!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11880"
msgstr "Mom! Dad!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11881"
msgstr "What's happening?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11882"
msgstr ""
"There's no time for questions!\n"
"Just carry them!\n"
"Carry them and go!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMarsStar07"
msgid "11883"
msgstr ""
"There's a space for you\n"
"to place something."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMarsStar08"
msgid "11884"
msgstr "{actor_name:5} got the Mars Star!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMarsStar09"
msgid "11885"
msgstr "{actor_name:5} used the Mars Star!"

msgctxt "MsgCheckedTheIce"
msgid "11886"
msgstr "{protagonist_name} checked the ice.{page_break}"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11887"
msgstr ""
"A shaft of ice is poking\n"
"up through the floor."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx80"
msgid "11888"
msgstr ""
"Thank you, {actor_name:5}.\n"
"And you, too, {actor_name:1}\n"
"and Kraden."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11889"
msgstr ""
"By igniting Mars Lighthouse,\n"
"you stopped Gaia Falls\n"
"from devouring our town."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11890"
msgstr ""
"We're just glad to have helped\n"
"save Weyard..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11891"
msgstr ""
"You've been through many\n"
"trials, more than any of us\n"
"can ever know..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11892"
msgstr ""
"We had no idea what to\n"
"expect when we lit the\n"
"final beacon..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11893"
msgstr ""
"When we saw the flash of\n"
"the beacon, we had no idea\n"
"what you suffered to light it..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11894"
msgstr ""
"I thought we were done for...\n"
"There was no way we could\n"
"escape with our parents' bodies."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11895"
msgstr ""
"Well, at least, not if we hadn't\n"
"pulled together and overcome\n"
"our sorrows..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11896"
msgstr "That light was brilliant!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11897"
msgstr ""
"You know, I shall always regret\n"
"that I didn't get to look upon\n"
"the beacon's light from afar..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11898"
msgstr ""
"I understand your regret... As\n"
"a scholar of Alchemy, you would\n"
"have been most impressed."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11899"
msgstr ""
"I saw the beams of blue, red,\n"
"and purple streaming out\n"
"toward the southeast..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11900"
msgstr ""
"That's the direction in which\n"
"Vale lies, is it not? Was the\n"
"light headed to your hometown?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11901"
msgstr ""
"Indeed it was. The Wise One\n"
"said the beams were going to\n"
"merge into one above Mt. Aleph."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11902"
msgstr ""
"The orb of golden light\n"
"we saw... That was shining\n"
"directly over Vale?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11903"
msgstr ""
"Yes. That was the Golden\n"
"Sun forming over Mt. Aleph."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11904"
msgstr ""
"If I remember the\n"
"tales correctly...{page_break}"
"The Golden Sun is the blast of\n"
"light emitted at the very moment\n"
"the Stone of Sages forms..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11905"
msgstr ""
"Such legends exist even\n"
"here? I wish that I'd known\n"
"that sooner!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11906"
msgstr ""
"I fear for Vale, to think that all\n"
"this energy is being released\n"
"right over your hometown."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11907"
msgstr ""
"We're all worried about that.\n"
"We're hoping we can return to\n"
"Vale as quickly as possible."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11908"
msgstr ""
"Oh... Is there nothing we can\n"
"do to convince you to stay?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11909"
msgstr ""
"We had hoped you might stay\n"
"in Prox a while, but that sounds\n"
"unlikely..."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11910"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry... We plan on\n"
"returning as soon as things\n"
"quiet down, don't we?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11911"
msgstr ""
"Our village will not soon forget\n"
"that you saved us from the edge\n"
"of destruction. Do visit us again."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11912"
msgstr ""
"You have just completed a\n"
"long and difficult journey.{page_break}"
"Perhaps when you are older,\n"
"and you look back on your youth,\n"
"you will remember us fondly..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11913"
msgstr ""
"When that time comes, I may\n"
"no longer be in this world."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11914"
msgstr ""
"Don't say such things... I'm\n"
"sure a long life awaits you."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11915"
msgstr ""
"Well, I suppose we should\n"
"be departing for Vale soon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11916"
msgstr ""
"You're right, Kraden...\n"
"If we don't, you-know-who\n"
"might start causing trouble..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11917"
msgstr ""
"At least some of your cares\n"
"have been remedied...{page_break}"
"You must be glad to know\n"
"we've brought all three\n"
"back from the brink of death."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11918"
msgstr ""
"I would not have thought it\n"
"possible had I not seen it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11919"
msgstr ""
"Even I do not fully\n"
"understand it..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11920"
msgstr ""
"But their can be no doubt. The\n"
"fire Psynergy released by the\n"
"beacon rekindled their spirits."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11921"
msgstr ""
"I hadn't expected so much\n"
"Psynergy to be released by\n"
"the lighthouse's beam..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11922"
msgstr ""
"I have no real explanation,\n"
"other than that their life force\n"
"had not been fully extinguished.{page_break}"
"It was a miracle, but the\n"
"fire Psynergy seems to have\n"
"recharged them somehow."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11923"
msgstr ""
"And had your parents not been\n"
"Adepts, the wave of Psynergy\n"
"would have passed them by."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11924"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}! What's taking you\n"
"two so long? Don't keep me\n"
"waiting!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11925"
msgstr ""
"Uh-oh! It's {actor_name:6}...\n"
"We're late, and she looks\n"
"rather displeased with us."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11926"
msgstr ""
"Should I let her know\n"
"we're leaving now?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11927"
msgstr ""
"I'm sorry! We're almost done.\n"
"Can you wait for us at the\n"
"village gates with the others?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11928"
msgstr ""
"I'm serious! If I have to wait\n"
"much longer, you're not\n"
"going to be happy!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11929"
msgstr ""
"I'm sorry, {actor_name:6}! It sounds\n"
"like things are going to take\n"
"just a little bit longer..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11930"
msgstr ""
"Well, I'm not going to wait much\n"
"longer! If you don't come soon,\n"
"we're all leaving without you!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11931"
msgstr "I'll wait outside with them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11932"
msgstr ""
"I don't think they want to\n"
"wait anymore, {actor_name:5}.\n"
"We're all set to head home..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11933"
msgstr ""
"They have no patience\n"
"whatsoever. Ah, well...\n"
"I suppose it is time to leave."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11934"
msgstr ""
"May your journey home\n"
"be safe and uneventful..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "11935"
msgstr ""
"We shall never forget what\n"
"you have done for Prox."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx81"
msgid "11936"
msgstr ""
"Thank you for lighting the\n"
"fires of the lighthouse beacon,\n"
"{actor_name:5}. You saved us all."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx82"
msgid "11937"
msgstr ""
"It's too bad about Agatio\n"
"and Karst...{page_break}"
"They weren't bad people... A\n"
"little obsessed, yeah, but it's\n"
"still sad that they're gone."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx83"
msgid "11938"
msgstr ""
"I don't remember the last\n"
"time I saw the sky this bright\n"
"and clear. It feels wonderful!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx84"
msgid "11939"
msgstr ""
"Winter in Prox can be bitter\n"
"cold, but I think things will\n"
"feel more mild after this."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx85"
msgid "11940"
msgstr ""
"I was so moved when I saw\n"
"that light shining from the\n"
"north. We all owe you our lives."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx86"
msgid "11941"
msgstr ""
"The lighthouses have all been\n"
"lit... Does that mean we're going\n"
"to fall back into war and chaos?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx87"
msgid "11942"
msgstr ""
"You did an amazing job... You\n"
"accomplished what Agatio and\n"
"Karst could not..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx88"
msgid "11943"
msgstr ""
"Will you be going back to Vale\n"
"now that your quest is over,\n"
"{actor_name:5}? Don't forget us!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx89"
msgid "11944"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5} has proven\n"
"himself as the strongest\n"
"warrior Prox has ever known!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx90"
msgid "11945"
msgstr ""
"I heard the Karst and Agatio\n"
"were defeated by a monstrous\n"
"dragon...{page_break}"
"{actor_name:5} beat the dragon,\n"
"though... I don't know whether\n"
"I'm impressed or scared of him."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx91"
msgid "11946"
msgstr ""
"The blizzard's finally over...\n"
"That was the worst patch of\n"
"weather we've ever had!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx92"
msgid "11947"
msgstr ""
"Now that our weather is\n"
"returning to normal, maybe\n"
"everyone will move back here."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx93"
msgid "11948"
msgstr ""
"I was the first person in town\n"
"to see the lighthouse! I was\n"
"so happy, I had to tell everyone!{page_break}"
"I felt like a little boy again,\n"
"running giddily through\n"
"town, shouting and waving!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx94"
msgid "11949"
msgstr ""
"They had no choice... They\n"
"had to light the four\n"
"elemental lighthouses...{page_break}"
"Even though it might mean\n"
"a rise in war and violence,\n"
"it had to be done."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx95"
msgid "11950"
msgstr ""
"When {actor_name:5} left town, he\n"
"of a fighter... He wasn't much\n"
"of anything, really...{page_break}"
"When did he become\n"
"mightier than the mightiest\n"
"of Prox's warriors?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx96"
msgid "11951"
msgstr ""
"I bet {actor_name:5} and his friends\n"
"live in a nice, warm place... I\n"
"wish I could go with them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx97"
msgid "11952"
msgstr ""
"I think the rift to the north\n"
"started receding when the\n"
"lighthouse was lit..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx98"
msgid "11953"
msgstr ""
"I wonder if that hole up\n"
"north has stopped growing...\n"
"What if it starts again?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx99"
msgid "11954"
msgstr ""
"The lighthouse was so beautiful\n"
"when the beacon was lit... It\n"
"made a beautiful band of light!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx100"
msgid "11955"
msgstr ""
"I was afraid the falls were\n"
"going to gobble me up!\n"
"I'm glad that's over now..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx101"
msgid "11956"
msgstr ""
"What do we do if the falls\n"
"start expanding again and\n"
"{actor_name:5} isn't here?{page_break}"
"Oh, great... That's going to\n"
"keep me up all night worrying."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx102"
msgid "11957"
msgstr ""
"All the lights joined up\n"
"together and shot off to\n"
"the southeast.{page_break}"
"It looked like they all\n"
"formed into a big, golden\n"
"ball or something."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx103"
msgid "11958"
msgstr ""
"I've been told that lighting\n"
"the four beacons has set\n"
"Alchemy free on the world.{page_break}"
"Now that we all can use\n"
"Alchemy again, civilization is\n"
"going to make great strides!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx104"
msgid "11959"
msgstr ""
"I guess the four lighthouses\n"
"were the seal that blocked\n"
"the power of Alchemy.{page_break}"
"So not only did {actor_name:5} save\n"
"Prox, he's also brought\n"
"about a new golden age!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx105"
msgid "11960"
msgstr ""
"The people of Prox won't\n"
"forget what you've done\n"
"for them...{page_break}"
"You can return home to\n"
"Vale with great pride, but you'll\n"
"always be welcome here."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx106"
msgid "11961"
msgstr ""
"Alchemy has been freed. We\n"
"must begin researching it\n"
"in earnest here in Prox."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx107"
msgid "11962"
msgstr ""
"Now that Alchemy is free,\n"
"it's like Weyard is waking up!\n"
"How will the world change?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx108"
msgid "11963"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5} and his allies\n"
"saved us from certain\n"
"destruction.{page_break}"
"It's a shame the rest of the\n"
"world doesn't know how much\n"
"they've done for us all."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx109"
msgid "11964"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, take some advice\n"
"from an old man...{page_break}"
"You would do well not to tell\n"
"anyone that you were the ones\n"
"to light the beacons..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx110"
msgid "11965"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1} and his friends left\n"
"Vale having sworn to return\n"
"with the Elemental Stars.{page_break}"
"When they return, they'll have\n"
"to tell everyone what happened.\n"
"I hope they won't be punished..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx111"
msgid "11966"
msgstr ""
"If they found out {actor_name:5} used\n"
"the treasures of Sol Sanctum\n"
"to light the beacons...{page_break}"
"That fool of a mayor would\n"
"no doubt punish them for\n"
"what they did to save us."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx112"
msgid "11967"
msgstr ""
"The mayor and the elders in\n"
"Vale are so out of touch.{page_break}"
"When they see {actor_name:5} and\n"
"his friends return without the\n"
"stones, they'll punish them."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx113"
msgid "11968"
msgstr ""
"Weeee! What fun! Now that\n"
"it's stopped snowing, we\n"
"can go outside and play."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx114"
msgid "11969"
msgstr ""
"I miss running around outside.\n"
"It's been so cold, I can't even\n"
"work up a good sweat."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx115"
msgid "11970"
msgstr ""
"If I'm going to be a great\n"
"warrior, like {actor_name:5}, I'm gonna\n"
"have to train hard."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx116"
msgid "11971"
msgstr ""
"I can hear the sound of\n"
"children playing far off\n"
"in the distance...{page_break}"
"That sound means that\n"
"everything's back to normal\n"
"and our worries are past."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx117"
msgid "11972"
msgstr ""
"Now that the lighthouse is lit,\n"
"we don't have to play in\n"
"that stupid igloo anymore."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx118"
msgid "11973"
msgstr ""
"That blizzard was unreal,\n"
"but it's gone now, and the\n"
"weather's beautiful."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx119"
msgid "11974"
msgstr ""
"You get more exercise running\n"
"in the snow, because it's a lot\n"
"harder to do."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx120"
msgid "11975"
msgstr ""
"It's been so long since\n"
"children's voices rang\n"
"through our streets.{page_break}"
"I hope these children\n"
"remain ignorant of how much\n"
"danger we were all in..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx121"
msgid "11976"
msgstr ""
"I have much to do, so I\n"
"won't be able to see you\n"
"off, but I wish you safe journey."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx122"
msgid "11977"
msgstr ""
"Your body has absorbed a\n"
"great deal of raw elemental\n"
"energy. Please be careful."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx123"
msgid "11978"
msgstr ""
"There's no telling what could\n"
"happen now... If you absorbed\n"
"energy, maybe {actor_name:6} did, too...{page_break}"
"Which means you'd better\n"
"not make her angry, or you'll\n"
"really get it!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx124"
msgid "11979"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, I always thought\n"
"of you as my very own grandson\n"
"when you were here...{page_break}"
"Now that you're leaving, I can't\n"
"describe the sorrow that fills\n"
"this old man's heart."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx125"
msgid "11980"
msgstr ""
"Think of your old grandma's\n"
"cooking every now and then\n"
"when you're back home in Vale."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx126"
msgid "11981"
msgstr ""
"We may have underestimated\n"
"the power of the Psynergy he\n"
"unleashed...{page_break}"
"We'll have to study it more\n"
"closely once we've seen\n"
"{actor_name:5} on his way."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx127"
msgid "11982"
msgstr ""
"The power to revive the dead...\n"
"It's an awesome and terrifying\n"
"power indeed...{page_break}"
"Eternal life could soon be in\n"
"the hands of Alchemists\n"
"everywhere... What a thought!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx128"
msgid "11983"
msgstr ""
"We've lost so many soldiers,\n"
"and now {actor_name:5} is leaving...\n"
"It's going to be quiet in Prox."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx129"
msgid "11984"
msgstr ""
"Who knew that the poor, injured\n"
"boy they brought back from Vale\n"
"would be the one to save Prox?{page_break}"
"I'm happy that he'll finally\n"
"be able to return home, but\n"
"I'll miss him so..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx130"
msgid "11985"
msgstr ""
"I'm so sad... {actor_name:5} doesn't\n"
"even have time to enjoy\n"
"this last meal I made him..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx131"
msgid "11986"
msgstr ""
"Thank you so much, {actor_name:5}!\n"
"If you hadn't returned to us,\n"
"we wouldn't be here now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx132"
msgid "11987"
msgstr ""
"Your foster grandmother knew\n"
"that you would return. She\n"
"always said you were reliable."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx133"
msgid "11988"
msgstr ""
"I never imagined that little\n"
"{actor_name:5} would become stronger\n"
"even than Agatio and Karst."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx134"
msgid "11989"
msgstr ""
"It's too bad {actor_name:5} can't\n"
"stick around... He'd make the\n"
"perfect son-in-law."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx135"
msgid "11990"
msgstr ""
"We had no idea there would\n"
"be such a terrible earthquake\n"
"when the beacon was lit.{page_break}"
"My wife tumbled right into my\n"
"arms... It was like we were\n"
"teenagers all over again!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx136"
msgid "11991"
msgstr ""
"After that earthquake, I feel\n"
"like I aged a couple of years\n"
"in just a few minutes!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx137"
msgid "11992"
msgstr ""
"We'll never be able to thank\n"
"{actor_name:5} and the warriors\n"
"of Vale enough.{page_break}"
"I hope they're all happy to\n"
"be home with their families\n"
"in Vale again."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx138"
msgid "11993"
msgstr ""
"When the earthquake hit,\n"
"{actor_name:5} and his friends\n"
"were high up on the lighthouse.{page_break}"
"If that had been me up there,\n"
"I think my heart would have\n"
"stopped from fear!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx139"
msgid "11994"
msgstr ""
"Now that the lighthouse has\n"
"been lit, I fear for what will\n"
"happen to Weyard."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx140"
msgid "11995"
msgstr ""
"The lighthouses are going\n"
"to restore the power of\n"
"Alchemy to the land...{page_break}"
"But Alchemy is too terrible\n"
"a power to set free..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx141"
msgid "11996"
msgstr ""
"Sorry, {actor_name:5}, but this road\n"
"is blocked off right now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx142"
msgid "11997"
msgstr ""
"If you're worried about the\n"
"lighthouse beacon, don't...\n"
"It's still lit."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx143"
msgid "11998"
msgstr ""
"I just don't think I'm cut out\n"
"to be a soldier. I should have\n"
"taken up knitting instead."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx144"
msgid "11999"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5} taught me a lot\n"
"about how to be a serious\n"
"soldier...{page_break}"
"I've been going easy on myself,\n"
"but no more! I'm going to train\n"
"harder every day!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx145"
msgid "12000"
msgstr ""
"Even just standing outside the\n"
"lighthouse, I can feel the energy\n"
"coming from within..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx146"
msgid "12001"
msgstr ""
"Well, you look like you're all\n"
"set for the return trip to Vale.\n"
"Travel well, {actor_name:5}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx147"
msgid "12002"
msgstr ""
"The road to the lighthouse\n"
"is in terrible shape after\n"
"the earthquake...{page_break}"
"I've got no clue how {actor_name:5}\n"
"and the others made it back\n"
"to town on that road."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx148"
msgid "12003"
msgstr ""
"The elders were saying that\n"
"the lighthouse beacon is tough\n"
"to put out once it's lit."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx149"
msgid "12004"
msgstr ""
"On the other hand, now that\n"
"Alchemy is free, maybe I\n"
"should study Alchemy..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx150"
msgid "12005"
msgstr ""
"Maybe if I train hard enough,\n"
"I'll be as strong as Menardi\n"
"and Karst were..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx151"
msgid "12006"
msgstr ""
"If the light of the beacon\n"
"keeps shining, the power\n"
"of Alchemy will never end...{page_break}"
"Even if Prox is attacked,\n"
"the bright flames of our\n"
"strength will burn on."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx152"
msgid "12007"
msgstr ""
"When {actor_name:5} left Prox, I didn't\n"
"think much of him, but now,\n"
"he's totally hot!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgProx153"
msgid "12008"
msgstr ""
"What took you so long?\n"
"Mom and Dad are tired\n"
"of waiting for you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12009"
msgstr ""
"That's not true, {actor_name:5}. You take\n"
"as long as you need to say\n"
"farewell to the people of Prox."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12010"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry about us, {actor_name:5}...\n"
"Puelle and the others took\n"
"good care of us."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12011"
msgstr ""
"Don't tell him that! We'll be\n"
"stuck here forever!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12012"
msgstr ""
"You look like you're feeling back\n"
"to your old self, {actor_name:6}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12013"
msgstr ""
"You were weeping such\n"
"mournful tears after the battle..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12014"
msgstr ""
"What!? As if!\n"
"You can't prove anything!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12015"
msgstr ""
"Go easy on her. You have to\n"
"remember, she thought that\n"
"both of her parents had died."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12016"
msgstr "Oh, were you crying, {actor_name:6}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12017"
msgstr ""
"No! I said...\n"
"I said I wasn't!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12018"
msgstr ""
"Now you've got me thinking\n"
"about my family... I didn't think\n"
"I'd miss them this much..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12019"
msgstr ""
"I only hope that they're all\n"
"safe back in Vale..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12020"
msgstr ""
"I just want to be home again...\n"
"I want to see how my mother\n"
"is doing..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12021"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry, Son. I'm sure\n"
"Dora's doing fine. She's a\n"
"strong woman."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12022"
msgstr ""
"But last time I saw her, she\n"
"looked so sick, so weak...{page_break}"
"Even if nothing happened\n"
"to Vale, I'm still worried..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12023"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry, {actor_name:1}. I'm sure\n"
"she's in wonderful shape.{page_break}"
"I think she'll be surprised\n"
"to see me!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12024"
msgstr ""
"And she wouldn't let anything\n"
"happen until you came home."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12025"
msgstr ""
"Sorry to keep you all waiting.\n"
"At last, the time has come for\n"
"us to return to Vale..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12026"
msgstr ""
"As soon as we leave Prox,\n"
"we'll head toward Angara, and\n"
"from there, to Vale..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12027"
msgstr ""
"I can't wait to see this\n"
"winged ship of yours! It\n"
"sounds so incredible!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12028"
msgstr ""
"I remember so little of our\n"
"trip to Prox... This is really\n"
"my first voyage on a ship."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12029"
msgstr ""
"I've heard that the wind and\n"
"waves make the boat rock...\n"
"I hope I don't get sick..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12030"
msgstr ""
"This ancient ship of ours\n"
"actually flies above the\n"
"ocean... It's quite a cozy ride."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12031"
msgstr ""
"It looks like we've got\n"
"an exciting last trip\n"
"ahead of us, doesn't it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12032"
msgstr ""
"Wow... Setting out like this\n"
"takes me back to our own\n"
"quest's start... It was so long ago."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12033"
msgstr ""
"I'm still worried about my\n"
"mother, but I'll try to put it\n"
"aside and enjoy the trip."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12034"
msgstr ""
"If you keep talking like this,\n"
"we'll never go anywhere!\n"
"Let's go, {actor_name:5}!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12035"
msgstr ""
"What's the matter, boys?\n"
"Are you reluctant to depart?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12036"
msgstr ""
"It's hard to believe that our\n"
"quest is almost at its end.\n"
"I know how you feel."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12037"
msgstr ""
"After all that we've been\n"
"through, you can't possibly be\n"
"nervous about this small trip!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12038"
msgstr ""
"I just hope that Vale came out\n"
"of this in as good a condition\n"
"as Prox did..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12039"
msgstr "We won't know until we get there."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12040"
msgstr ""
"I can't stop thinking about\n"
"how my parents are doing..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12041"
msgstr "Were the both of them in Vale?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12042"
msgstr ""
"Can't you make a guess, Kraden?\n"
"Will Vale still be standing\n"
"when we arrive?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12043"
msgstr "Not even I can know that..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12044"
msgstr ""
"I can see it in your eyes,\n"
"Kraden! You think something's\n"
"happened, don't you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12045"
msgstr ""
"It's a possibility... One that\n"
"cannot be ignored..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12046"
msgstr ""
"If it's not there, then what's\n"
"the point in even going back?"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12047"
msgstr ""
"Is that really how you\n"
"feel, {actor_name:1}? What about\n"
"you, {actor_name:5}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12048"
msgstr ""
"Have you already forgotten all\n"
"that we discussed? You ought\n"
"to refresh your memory!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12049"
msgstr ""
"You remember, don't you,\n"
"{actor_name:5}? Think about it\n"
"for a moment, {actor_name:1}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12050"
msgstr "What do you mean?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12051"
msgstr ""
"Our conversation with Hamma\n"
"after we ignited the beacon..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12052"
msgstr ""
"Don't you remember us talking\n"
"to the children from Imil at the\n"
"base of Mercury Lighthouse?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12053"
msgstr ""
"When they were warning people\n"
"away from the lighthouses?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12054"
msgstr ""
"Yes. The Wise One instructed\n"
"everyone to seek refuge."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12055"
msgstr "Yeah, so what about it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12056"
msgstr "You still don't see, {actor_name:2}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12057"
msgstr ""
"Even if Vale were destroyed,\n"
"I'd expect that the villagers\n"
"have all escaped to safety."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12058"
msgstr ""
"I guess that's true... They\n"
"might still be all right."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12059"
msgstr ""
"That's true... So whatever\n"
"happens, my family's alive!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12060"
msgstr ""
"I'd forgotten about that...\n"
"Thanks, Kraden."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12061"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:2}, can you make sure\n"
"everyone else knows that?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12062"
msgstr ""
"OK, let's go. The both of you!\n"
"We have to catch up to\n"
"everyone."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12063"
msgstr "Kraden..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12064"
msgstr ""
"Why did the Wise One change\n"
"our parents into a dragon? Why\n"
"did he make us fight them?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12065"
msgstr ""
"I mean, we almost killed them...\n"
"He tried to make us kill our\n"
"own parents. Why?"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12066"
msgstr ""
"Do you think that he intended\n"
"for them to die from the start?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12067"
msgstr ""
"I cannot speak for him, but I\n"
"think he knew that they would\n"
"be revived by the beacon's light."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12068"
msgstr ""
"Ah... You don't understand why\n"
"he put you through all this if\n"
"he knew they'd survive..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12069"
msgstr ""
"We cannot hope to fathom the\n"
"motives of a being as all-\n"
"powerful as the Wise One..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12070"
msgstr "You don't know either, Kraden?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12071"
msgstr ""
"I can only hazard a guess...\n"
"The Wise One...\n"
"wanted to test you."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12072"
msgstr "What do you mean, test us?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12073"
msgstr ""
"I cannot tell you more... It is\n"
"up to you to find the answer."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12074"
msgstr ""
"Will we use Alchemy to wage\n"
"war, to raise armies?{page_break}"
"Or will we use it to grow wise,\n"
"to rise above our petty feuds\n"
"and perform great deeds?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12075"
msgstr ""
"You were willing to sacrifice\n"
"everything for your quest. I'd say\n"
"you've risen to this challenge."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12076"
msgstr ""
"Oops! Is everyone else that\n"
"far ahead of us?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12077"
msgstr ""
"We'd better hurry and catch\n"
"up to the others before they\n"
"leave us behind!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12078"
msgstr ""
"After all, I'm not terribly\n"
"interested in trying to walk\n"
"all the way back to Vale."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12079"
msgstr ""
"If you feel the same, then\n"
"we'd better be hurrying."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12080"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}! {actor_name:5}!\n"
"We're off!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShipIceWallFirstApproach"
msgid "12081"
msgstr ""
"Kraden, come look at this...\n"
"There's a huge ice wall\n"
"blocking our path..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12082"
msgstr ""
"Hm... If we can't do something\n"
"about that wall, we're not going\n"
"any farther, {actor_name:5}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShipIceWallCrewReposition"
msgid "12083"
msgstr ""
"Kraden, come look at this...\n"
"There's a huge ice wall\n"
"blocking our path..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12084"
msgstr ""
"Nothing to worry about,\n"
"{actor_name:6}. We'll just have to\n"
"use that cannon we got in Loho!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12085"
msgstr ""
"That's right! If the cannon can\n"
"blast away a stone wall, think\n"
"what it'll do to ice!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12086"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:5}, take us between those\n"
"two blocks of ice for shelter\n"
"when you fire the cannon."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgShipSafeFiringDistance"
msgid "12087"
msgstr ""
"We should be safe if we\n"
"fire from this distance."

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12088"
msgstr ""
"OK, here we go! {actor_name:5}, aim\n"
"right at the ice wall and fire\n"
"when ready!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12089"
msgstr ""
"What? You're not ready yet?\n"
"Take your time and get\n"
"into position then...{page_break}"
"But as soon as you're\n"
"ready, fire!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12090"
msgstr "Fire the Magma Ball!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12091"
msgstr ""
"Great! We did it! We\n"
"can keep going now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12092"
msgstr ""
"All right, let's head for\n"
"the Northern Seas."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12093"
msgstr "Let's go!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgGoldenSunFormation"
msgid "12094"
msgstr ""
"The Golden Sun... The very\n"
"quintessence of Alchemy's\n"
"power! It's beginning!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12095"
msgstr ""
"Wait for me! Please, wait!\n"
"Wait until I reach the\n"
"summit of Mt. Aleph!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgGoldenSunEternalLifeAndPower"
msgid "12096"
msgstr ""
"At last! I have it!\n"
"Eternal life...and\n"
"limitless power!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12097"
msgstr ""
"At last, the power of nature\n"
"is mine to control as I will!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12098"
msgstr ""
"Rise, storms! Rise up and\n"
"unleash your might upon Vale\n"
"and the foothills of Mt. Aleph!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12099"
msgstr ""
"That's odd... I should have\n"
"limitless power... So why can't\n"
"I call up a simple storm?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12100"
msgstr "Wh-Who are you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12101"
msgstr "I am called the Wise One..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12102"
msgstr "The Wise One? Vale's protector?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12103"
msgstr "You wish to have limitless power?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12104"
msgstr ""
"Wish to?\n"
"I just got it!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12105"
msgstr ""
"No. Your power is nearly\n"
"limitless, but it has boundaries."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12106"
msgstr ""
"Nearly limitless? You speak\n"
"in riddles. Can't you see?\n"
"The power is mine!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12107"
msgstr ""
"Yes. You also have nearly endless\n"
"life. And your Psynergy is...\n"
"somewhat stronger."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12108"
msgstr ""
"If you are trying to anger me,\n"
"have a little taste of exactly how\n"
"much power I have attained!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12109"
msgstr ""
"Look at me! My body is\n"
"brimming with power!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12110"
msgstr ""
"How!? What's going on?\n"
"I should be all-powerful!\n"
"How can you defeat me?!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12111"
msgstr ""
"You are not all-powerful, Alex.\n"
"Your power has its limits, as\n"
"does your life."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12112"
msgstr ""
"That cannot be! Who is\n"
"responsible for this treachery?\n"
"Who has robbed me of my dream?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12113"
msgstr ""
"I, the Wise One, imbued the Mars\n"
"Star with some of the power\n"
"of the forming Golden Sun.{page_break}"
"It rests even now in the hands\n"
"of young {actor_name:1}."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12114"
msgstr "Why?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12115"
msgstr ""
"The heavens and earth are\n"
"changing, Alex! You must\n"
"flee{pause_20_skippable} now!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12116"
msgstr "Wha-What!?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12117"
msgstr ""
"Mt. Aleph will soon be drawn\n"
"into the heart of the earth! You\n"
"must flee or join it forever!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12118"
msgstr ""
"Flee?! I can't flee!{pause_20_skippable}\n"
"I can't even move!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12119"
msgstr ""
"Ah, yes. You now see the limits of\n"
"your power. If you are swallowed\n"
"by the earth, you may not survive."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12120"
msgstr ""
"If you survive, perhaps we\n"
"shall meet again someday..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMadraInteriors165"
msgid "12121"
msgstr ""
"We're heading to Tolbi. We hear\n"
"there's a tournament there\n"
"called Colosso.{page_break}"
"I'm Morgan, and this here's\n"
"Dekka. We're gonna compete,\n"
"and we're gonna win!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMadraInteriors166"
msgid "12122"
msgstr ""
"Hey, if you see a gladiator\n"
"named {actor_name:1}, give him\n"
"a message for me...{page_break}"
"If he's thinking about going\n"
"to Colosso this year, he doesn't\n"
"stand a chance of winning!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMadraInteriors167"
msgid "12123"
msgstr ""
"The gladiator who takes the\n"
"prize in Colosso earns quite\n"
"a reputation as a warrior...{page_break}"
"Mercenaries get a lot more\n"
"jobs when they've got a\n"
"good reputation."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgMadraInteriors168"
msgid "12124"
msgstr ""
"We fought in Colosso last\n"
"year, but we lost to a weaselly\n"
"little kid named {actor_name:1}.{page_break}"
"We're after revenge, so we've\n"
"been out on a risky journey to\n"
"increase our fighting strength."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgIFound2"
msgid "12125"
msgstr "I found {actor_name:1}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12126"
msgstr ""
"We've been looking for\n"
"you, {actor_name:1}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12127"
msgstr "Who are you guys?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12128"
msgstr ""
"The name's Satrage. You\n"
"took me out in the last\n"
"round at Colosso."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12129"
msgstr "And I'm Azart!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12130"
msgstr "And don't forget Navampa!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12131"
msgstr "Oh. It's you guys."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12132"
msgstr ""
"Is that any way to say\n"
"hello to some old friends?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12133"
msgstr "What's your problem?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12134"
msgstr ""
"We want to talk to you\n"
"about your fighting style\n"
"at Colosso."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12135"
msgstr ""
"Yeah. And we think you shouldn't\n"
"have won, {actor_name:1}. We think\n"
"you didn't fight fair."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12136"
msgstr ""
"It sounds like you resent the\n"
"fact that {actor_name:1} beat you..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12137"
msgstr ""
"We've just been thinking about\n"
"it, and there's no way that\n"
"{actor_name:1} should have won!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12138"
msgstr ""
"Right. So you think I cheated\n"
"just because I used my\n"
"Pynergy abilities in Colosso?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12139"
msgstr ""
"I don't know how you did\n"
"it. I'm just sayin' I think\n"
"you cheated is all..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12140"
msgstr ""
"Ah, but Psynergy is a warrior's\n"
"skill, every bit as much as your\n"
"sword arts. It isn't cheating."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12141"
msgstr ""
"You're not listening, are you,\n"
"old man? That fight was fixed,\n"
"and we're here to pay you back!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgHeyTheseGuys"
msgid "12142"
msgstr ""
"Hey, these guys aren't\n"
"very strong at all!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12143"
msgstr ""
"Ha! We were right! They\n"
"{text_effect:2}were{reset_text_style} cheating at Colosso!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12144"
msgstr "I knew it!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12145"
msgstr ""
"It takes a lot to reach the\n"
"finals at Colosso... A lot more\n"
"than you guys can take."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12146"
msgstr ""
"You look like you've got\n"
"business in here, but there's\n"
"no way you're getting past us."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12147"
msgstr ""
"Give it up! We're staying here.\n"
"We've got our eyes peeled, and\n"
"there's no way you're getting in!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgTheseGuysWere"
msgid "12148"
msgstr "These guys were phenomenal!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12149"
msgstr ""
"Which one of you didn't think\n"
"they won Colosso fair and\n"
"square?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12150"
msgstr ""
"It wasn't me! I think both you\n"
"and Navampa were saying\n"
"something like that."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12151"
msgstr ""
"So. You don't still think our\n"
"victory at Colosso was fixed,\n"
"do you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12152"
msgstr ""
"No way, {actor_name:1}! We've seen\n"
"the error of our ways!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12153"
msgstr ""
"We promise we won't badmouth\n"
"you or call you a fraud ever\n"
"again. Will you forgive us?"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12154"
msgstr ""
"Don't be that way! We've\n"
"learned our lesson! Forgive us!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12155"
msgstr ""
"You're not such a bad\n"
"kid after all!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12156"
msgstr ""
"You came out here looking\n"
"for treasure, didn't you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12157"
msgstr ""
"Here, this was in the chest\n"
"we found."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12158"
msgstr ""
"You were nice enough to\n"
"forgive us, so we think you\n"
"should have it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12159"
msgstr ""
"Right, well... I guess we'll\n"
"be leaving now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12160"
msgstr ""
"By the time the next Colosso\n"
"rolls around, we ought to be\n"
"strong enough to win for sure!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12161"
msgstr "Maybe we'll see you there."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgChampa52"
msgid "12162"
msgstr "{actor_name:1}!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12163"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1}, is it you? Do my\n"
"eyes deceive me?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12164"
msgstr "Oh. I must have been mistaken."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12165"
msgstr ""
"No, you are not\n"
"{actor_name:1}, are you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12166"
msgstr ""
"Young lady, are you looking\n"
"for someone by the name\n"
"of {actor_name:1}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12167"
msgstr ""
"Yes, old man! I am looking\n"
"for one called {actor_name:1}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12168"
msgstr "Where is {actor_name:1}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12169"
msgstr ""
"I'm sorry... {actor_name:1} isn't\n"
"with us..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12170"
msgstr ""
"Well then, where can I\n"
"find {actor_name:1}?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12171"
msgstr ""
"Why do you want to find\n"
"him so badly?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12172"
msgstr ""
"Me? I am Feizhi... {actor_name:1}\n"
"helped me once."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12173"
msgstr ""
"He helped Ulmuch. Ulmuch was\n"
"trapped, but {actor_name:1} saved him.\n"
"He is a brave man, isn't he?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12174"
msgstr ""
"I suppose... But why are you\n"
"looking for him? Do you{pause_20_skippable}\n"
"like him? Is that it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12175"
msgstr ""
"You're a mean old man. It is\n"
"not polite to tease me."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12176"
msgstr ""
"That's what it is! You\n"
"like {actor_name:1}!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12177"
msgstr "No! I am so embarrassed!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12178"
msgstr ""
"Don't worry, Feizhi... We'll tell\n"
"{actor_name:1} how you feel!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12179"
msgstr "I...{pause_20_skippable} Really?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12180"
msgstr ""
"Then...will you give him\n"
"this when you tell him?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12181"
msgstr "What is it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12182"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1} is on a dangerous\n"
"journey. I am worried about him,\n"
"so I made him a good luck charm."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12183"
msgstr "Ah, a good luck charm... I see."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12184"
msgstr ""
"I am going home now, old man.\n"
"Thank you for doing this favor\n"
"for me."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgAlhafraInteriors120"
msgid "12185"
msgstr ""
"Legends said that Crossbone\n"
"Isle could be found in the\n"
"middle of the Karagol Sea."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12186"
msgstr ""
"Ah... Crossbone Isle... Wait,\n"
"did you say \"could\"? Is it not\n"
"there anymore or something?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12187"
msgstr ""
"Well, it's still there, but there's\n"
"no point in going. Someone\n"
"named {actor_name:1} picked it clean."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12188"
msgstr "What, he took all the treasure?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12189"
msgstr ""
"Yeah. And apparently, he\n"
"even defeated the ancient\n"
"ghost pirate protecting it..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12190"
msgstr ""
"What about the stories that if you\n"
"beat the ghost pirate, you would\n"
"become the leader of all pirates?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12191"
msgstr ""
"Well, you see, that means that\n"
"{actor_name:1} is our leader now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12192"
msgstr ""
"Wow... just like that?{pause_20_skippable} I'll bet\n"
"he's pretty tough."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12193"
msgstr ""
"No doubt. But you know, he\n"
"must be a reliable guy, too..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12194"
msgstr "You think?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12195"
msgstr ""
"You'd have to be to beat that\n"
"ghost. That's why we're looking\n"
"for him now, remember?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12196"
msgstr ""
"If he's looking for a pirate\n"
"crew, he can count me in!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgHeyWaitA"
msgid "12197"
msgstr "Hey! Wait a minute!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12198"
msgstr "Who are you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12199"
msgstr ""
"You were talking about\n"
"{actor_name:1}, weren't you?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12200"
msgstr ""
"Don't play dumb...\n"
"We all heard you."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12201"
msgstr ""
"Yes, we know {actor_name:1}.\n"
"What about him?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12202"
msgstr ""
"Well, why don't you tell us\n"
"where we can find him?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12203"
msgstr ""
"Why should we tell\n"
"you anything?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12204"
msgstr ""
"{actor_name:1} took good care of\n"
"us when we were in Vault, and\n"
"we'd like to thank him..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12205"
msgstr ""
"Ah, yes... Well... I'm afraid\n"
"we don't know where you can\n"
"find {actor_name:1} right now."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12206"
msgstr ""
"Oh, is that so? Well, I guess\n"
"we'll just have to give you the\n"
"reward we'd planned for him."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12207"
msgstr ""
"You've got a grudge against\n"
"{actor_name:1}, and you're going\n"
"to take it out on us?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12208"
msgstr ""
"Oh yeah, you could call it\n"
"a grudge... A serious grudge."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12209"
msgstr ""
"But don't worry... We're just\n"
"going to give you a little sample\n"
"of what we've planned for him."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgItLooksLike"
msgid "12210"
msgstr ""
"It looks like {actor_name:1} runs\n"
"with a pretty feeble crowd..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12211"
msgstr ""
"Well, we have been working out.\n"
"Maybe {actor_name:1} won't be so\n"
"tough this time around..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12212"
msgstr ""
"So you think we just\n"
"got a lot stronger?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12213"
msgstr ""
"You let {actor_name:1} know\n"
"we're looking for him!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12214"
msgstr ""
"The band of thieves he busted\n"
"in Vault are coming to repay\n"
"the favor!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12215"
msgstr "And we're not messing around!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12216"
msgstr ""
"Be sure you tell him!\n"
"And send him this way!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgWeLostAgain"
msgid "12217"
msgstr "We lost again..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12218"
msgstr ""
"So, boss... You, uh... You think\n"
"maybe it was a mistake going\n"
"after these guys?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12219"
msgstr ""
"This means we're going to\n"
"jail again, doesn't it?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12220"
msgstr ""
"Aw... Why do we have to go\n"
"back to jail. I hate it there..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12221"
msgstr ""
"It's not like we really hurt\n"
"anyone... After all, we lost!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12222"
msgstr ""
"Yeah... And it's not like we\n"
"stole anything...this time..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12223"
msgstr ""
"We're not gonna have to\n"
"go to jail, are we?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12224"
msgstr "You're thieves!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12225"
msgstr ""
"If we asked around, we could\n"
"probably find a dozen reasons\n"
"to have you locked up!"

#, alchemy-end-now
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12226"
msgstr ""
"Are you guys, like, wandering\n"
"sheriffs or something?"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12227"
msgstr ""
"Because we could be really\n"
"useful to you if you are. We know\n"
"all sorts of criminal elements..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12228"
msgstr ""
"And even if you're not, we\n"
"could be really useful to you...\n"
"Anything's better than jail!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12229"
msgstr ""
"You can't honestly believe\n"
"we would let you join us!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12230"
msgstr ""
"Hey, come on! We haven't done\n"
"anything wrong, really! Not yet,\n"
"anyway..."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12231"
msgstr ""
"Yeah! We didn't have enough\n"
"time to do anything bad before\n"
"we ran into you guys!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12232"
msgstr "Yeah, so give us a break!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12233"
msgstr "So, uh... Bye! See you later!"

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12234"
msgstr ""
"Will you promise to stop\n"
"following {actor_name:1} and trying\n"
"to get revenge on him?"

msgctxt "message"
msgid "12235"
msgstr ""
"The four elements are\n"
"the basic building\n"
"blocks of all matter.{page_break}"
"The elemental spirits\n"
"are called Djinn.{page_break}"
"The four elements are\n"
"Venus for Earth,\n"
"Mercury for Water,{page_break}"
"Mars for Fire, and\n"
"Jupiter for Wind.{page_break}"
"Each element has many\n"
"different Djinn."

msgctxt "message"
msgid "12236"
msgstr ""
"When you set a Djinni, its\n"
"elemental power may\n"
"change your class{page_break}"
"or Psynergy. In battle,\n"
"you can unleash the\n"
"powers of set Djinn."

msgctxt "message"
msgid "12237"
msgstr ""
"When a Djinni is standing\n"
"by, you can use it\n"
"to summon in battle.{page_break}"
"To use a summon\n"
"immediately, put your\n"
"Djinn on standby before{page_break}"
"battle. But be careful,\n"
"because changing set\n"
"Djinn to standby changes{page_break}"
"your class and Psynergy."

msgctxt "message"
msgid "12238"
msgstr ""
"If you have a standby\n"
"Djinni in battle, you\n"
"can use it to summon.{page_break}"
"After summoning, the\n"
"Djinni will be in\n"
"recovery until it has{page_break}"
"recovered all its\n"
"power. Recovering Djinni\n"
"cannot be unleashed{page_break}"
"or used to summon."

msgctxt "message"
msgid "12239"
msgstr ""
"If a Djinni's power is\n"
"used to summon, the\n"
"Djinni enters recovery.{page_break}"
"After it has recovered\n"
"its power, it will set\n"
"itself once again."

msgctxt "message"
msgid "12240"
msgstr ""
"When a Djinni is set to\n"
"an Adept, its power\n"
"may change the Adept's{page_break}"
"class. Find your own\n"
"unique combinations of\n"
"Djinni to improve your{page_break}"
"characters' classes."

msgctxt "message"
msgid "12241"
msgstr ""
"Psynergy is a mental\n"
"power. People who wield\n"
"it are called Adepts.{page_break}"
"Psynergy can change\n"
"with class changes or\n"
"when you go up a level.{page_break}"
"Try changing your\n"
"class to earn new\n"
"Psynergy."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "MsgDjinnGiveTutorialA"
msgid "12242"
msgstr ""
"To give your Djinni to\n"
"someone else, move it\n"
"like this."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12243"
msgstr ""
"After choosing who gets the\n"
"Djinni, you can \"set\" it."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12244"
msgstr ""
"When your class changes,\n"
"the Psynergy you can use\n"
"may also change."

#, alchemy-end-wait
msgctxt "message"
msgid "12245"
msgstr ""
